{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting","id":265726,"title":"Back and looking to play: Skype game recruiting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-25T14:08:38-07:00","id":265726,"title":"Back and looking to play: Skype game recruiting","content":"Things have been abit messy, come back to find a new forum but figure I'd just dive back in anyways and assume no new etiquette had been added that I am aware of.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>WHERE</b></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Game will</span> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">be held over skype voice chat cause while I do enjoy a nice text based adventure I've grown more fond of talking to human beings instead of just reading what they write. Hopefully I'm not in the minority.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>WHEN</u></b></span></span></span><br /> Thinking Friday evening. I figure that would be when most people are free but if you are interested please list when you can and cannot play.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>WHAT</b></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Exalted 2e. Will detail rule adjustments and stuff if people are interested. The story will start basic so we can focus more on building the characters up and getting you invested. However I do eventually plan on using my Devourer campaign setting. Those of you that remember the old forum may recall this setting as the one with the unknown army wiping out existence. It originated from the wyld but those that escaped say it is completely alien to the fae.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>WHO </u></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">All solaroids (though no broken wing crane for infernals, sorry), if you wish to play sidereal, lunar, or alchemic you can but things will be balanced for solar teir so keep that in mind.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>WHY</b></u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Because the game will be awesome</span></span><br /> <br /> <u><b>Player Characters</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodless</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mayu </a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_kLDAvk555Q0VWcVJ0aWlSajQ/view\" target=\"_blank\">Alric</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>NPCs</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Embers upon the Snow</b><br /> - Allegiance: The Lover<br /> - Alias: Unknown<br /> - Splat: Moonshadow abyssal<br /> - Notes: Wields flamepieces, hyper-violent, can speak non-verbally<br /> <br /> <b>Korac</b><br /> - Allegiance: The Lover, Tear Eaters<br /> - Alias: unknown<br /> - Splat: Ghost<br /> - Notes: Cunning, diplomatic<br /> <br /> <b>The Bartender</b><br /> - Allegiance: The Lover, Tear Eaters<br /> - Alias: Unknown<br /> - Splat: Unknown<br /> - Notes: Thurmaturge, teleportation, aloof, makes really good hot chocolate<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Dice Roller<br /> <a href=\"https://rolz.org/group\" target=\"_blank\">https://rolz.org/group</a></u></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3945,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","user":"Aeroz","date":". 02-15-2015, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T14:18:57-07:00","id":265746,"title":"","content":"Friday evening in which timezone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T14:23:29-07:00","id":265752,"title":"","content":"And is this a one night campaign or how often would you like to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T14:25:53-07:00","id":265755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=265746#post265746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friday evening in which timezone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ninja'd!<br /> <br /> And how broken/optimised/min-maxed a character can I make? No BWC, but any other off-limits sources? Lords of Creation? Scroll of Swallowed Darkness? Which artifact rules are we using (Core? Wonders? Codex?)? Custom manses? Custom charms? How will Player NPCs work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:01:41-07:00","id":265776,"title":"","content":"All of the above. Also, color me interested!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:12:50-07:00","id":265780,"title":"","content":"I am EST, though am flexible on time. If most people was on the west coast I dont mind starting the game in what I'd consider later. I'd aim for about 8 or 9pm EST but that is flexible by a few hours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=265755#post265755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ninja'd!<br /> <br /> And how broken/optimised/min-maxed a character can I make? No BWC, but any other off-limits sources? Lords of Creation? Scroll of Swallowed Darkness? Which artifact rules are we using (Core? Wonders? Codex?)? Custom manses? Custom charms? How will Player NPCs work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok since there is interest I will get into some of this, keep in mind I haven't been around in over two years so forgive me if things have changed.<br /> <br /> No Flaws or Merits<br /> I like this system, I really do but its too easy to break the game to allow it for a new group<br /> <br /> Errata<br /> Sure its changed, but last I checked the tweaks were good enough for me to default to using it.<br /> <br /> Banned Books<br /> No Lords of Creation, between me not having it and it having quite a few unbalanced artifacts and charms I'm saying no on it. Scroll of Swallowed Darkness? If you really want, sure go ahead. But keep the temperment of the group in mind. If I have to I will do a mid-game ruling if the material makes people uncomfortable. <br /> <br /> Artifacts<br /> I tend to be stricter on individual artifacts the more standard they are. Grand daiklaive and power armor will not go over well, Resplendant recorder or perfect boots I will pretty much always give a pass on. I also dont consider &quot;I found a manse full of stuff&quot; to be legitimate justification on why you have 10 dots of artifacts. The rules for making them will be a modified version of the codex emphasizing the journey of its creation. In other words I want to focus on you RPing the process and care far more about that than you running all over creation for something specific.<br /> <br /> Perfect Defenses<br /> I go with these limitations. To dodge you must have somewhere to dodge too, to parry it must be something parry-able. Stunting can get around these limitations, in practice it just means you'll have to put some thought into it.and not blindly rely on it.<br /> <br /> Stunting<br /> You wont get motes for this. One die just means putting in some effort to RP. Two die is creative use of whats around you. Three die is doing something especially awesome. If you do a three die stunt in addition to the regular perks everyone will get bonus exp.<br /> <br /> Homebrew<br /> I do allow it but not to start, if you some how find my homebrew like Paper Crane Style or Party Cannon you can use that too<br /> <br /> Min/Max<br /> A degree to twinking is ok but if you are nothing but one and five dots there will be some issues. Also use logic, like I dont care how much of a military genius your dynast prodigy is there is no way your family would let you get away with zero lore and war. This is as much for the players as balance. I tend to throw out threats where &quot;hit it until it dies&quot; mentality will get you killed. Basic knowledge of things will give you more options and make it less likely to die from an overlooked threat. I wont fault you for having stats you really care about with five dots, but I will if your entire sheet has your character as a complete master or novice with no middle ground.<br /> <br /> Thats all the stuff that comes to mind right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:19:33-07:00","id":265782,"title":"","content":"Voice chat, my eternal nemesiiiiiis","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:28:04-07:00","id":265785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=265780#post265780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stunting<br /> You wont get motes for this. One die just means putting in some effort to RP. Two die is creative use of whats around you. Three die is doing something especially awesome. If you do a three die stunt in addition to the regular perks everyone will get bonus exp.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No motes gained back? I'm not sure how I feel about that. What about willpower?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm on mountain standard time. And you didn't say how often you would like to play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:45:36-07:00","id":265810,"title":"","content":"No mote regain is a very, very harsh rule. Dare I suggest go with 3e's solution of flat regen of 5/turn? Even 2 or 3 should be doable, 0 is killer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T17:09:16-07:00","id":265819,"title":"","content":"Game would be weekly.<br /> <br /> Now I am a GM that tries to put player enjoyment first. I find mote regen just drags out fights and makes things antagonistic between player and GM &quot;WHAT DO YOU MEAN I DONT GET STUNT DICE, I NEED THOSE MOTES&quot; situations. <br /> <br /> But if everyone wants it, I will have mote regen under the understanding that if that kind of thing starts happening I will pull it. I want players to view stunting as a nice bonus not something that should be handed to them each turn. Oh and to be clear stunt dice for multiple actions is a pool you divide how you see fit, not full amount to every action. <br /> <br /> Regardless though I am keeping willpower rewards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:04:07-07:00","id":265833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=265819#post265819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I am a GM that tries to put player enjoyment first. I find mote regen just drags out fights and makes things antagonistic between player and GM &quot;WHAT DO YOU MEAN I DONT GET STUNT DICE, I NEED THOSE MOTES&quot; situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is more a problem with player attitudes than anything else. But I do see where you are coming from. A general understanding of each other and that you're the ST, a general level of cooperation should be had, even when there are disagreements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T01:36:09-07:00","id":266050,"title":"","content":"mark me down as interested<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T07:13:39-07:00","id":266134,"title":"","content":"Your proposal sounds very much like what I was looking for. I'm in EST, free Friday nights and like playing Solars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have questions off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. When Ex3 comes out, will we make the switch (at some point, not necessarily launch day)?<br /> 2. What's the tone/adult level of the campaign? I've tried to join an online Exalted campaign before, but it ended up more Exxxalted than blood and sandals. I'm looking for champions of creation doing epic deeds, not all-ERP all the time.<br /> 3. Is this video skype or voice skype (cool either way, but might need to dig up a camera)<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T09:44:46-07:00","id":266242,"title":"","content":"Another quick rule than a text dump.<br /> BACKGROUNDS<br /> Exp will not be gained or lost for backgrounds gained or lost during role playing but will be if it occurs during downtime. So if we play out a scene where your player convinces freed slaves to join him you get them at no cost. If I ask &quot;what are you doing for the next week while your sorcerer prepares to summon a demon&quot; and you say recruit followers at the inn that will cost exp. On the flip side if in a fight someone manages to knock your daiklave into a volcano (and assuming you dont have a way to get it back) than you dont gain exp.<br /> <br /> Gonna re-write opening post to get this all down. Since no one expressed specific times I'll go with friday 8pm EST. This can be adjusted if another time works better.<br /> <br /> I have a 3 player minimum for games 7 max. If 7 seems abit high its because with a new group its common for one or two people to drop early on. I know how eager people can be so we might start next week if that works for everyone.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask any questions, my skype is aerozord if you guys need to discuss anything.<br /> <br /> I will also say one more thing because its come up as an issue and I want to be clear. There will be no GM transparency. You wont know the numerical results of rolls, I will not detail limitations of homebrew enemies or how to kill them, or give you any information that your player would not know. For this to work players will have to trust me to be fair and do what I feel makes for a good story. You will not always win fights, there will be times the correct course of action is to run. Followers can die, possessions destroyed, characters maimed. I might give some plot armor if its a big part of your character and played as such. For example your character intends to use his family daiklave to avenge his father, that is something I'd be less inclined to destroy even if its logical for an enemy to do so but I expect that to be played up and your character to also pass up better weapon. You need to show that specific artifact is important to the story.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266134#post266134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your proposal sounds very much like what I was looking for. I'm in EST, free Friday nights and like playing Solars. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have questions off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. When Ex3 comes out, will we make the switch (at some point, not necessarily launch day)?<br /> 2. What's the tone/adult level of the campaign? I've tried to join an online Exalted campaign before, but it ended up more Exxxalted than blood and sandals. I'm looking for champions of creation doing epic deeds, not all-ERP all the time.<br /> 3. Is this video skype or voice skype (cool either way, but might need to dig up a camera)<br /> <br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Depends on how easy the conversion would be, how far along we are ect. What little I've seen of 3e (and keep in mind I have been out of the loop for awhile) is much of the stuff I tweak anyways when it comes to lore. Sadly the only real answer I can give is we'll have to wait and see when it comes out.<br /> <br /> 2. I hope this doesn't turn anyone off but, this will be a heroic story. Atleast what passes as heroic in Exalted. Few things bore me as quickly as running a game full of complete sociopaths. Thats the group as a whole. I'm ok if your character thinks slavery is ok or that violently torturing someone to death is acceptable because you need to get to the underworld ASAP to save a village, but I want death and suffering to have weight and that means the group as a whole needs to care.<br /> <br /> This means a fairly serious game. I do expect and want some light-hearted fun too. Need to juxtapose all that drama. What I really mean is I expect players to take the game seriously and become invested. I will give fair warning I know how to poke and prod players. Last time I had a group in the underworld one of our solars ended up in the fetal position. In another I ran a player character snapped, going &quot;its fine its fine, I'll just blow up everything and then it will be fine, ITS FINE.&quot; I like things like that, makes games memorable.<br /> <br /> I know that wasn't what you were primarily asking but I knew I had to explain all that anyways so though this was a good time. Adult content, well one upside to voice chat is people tend not be as gratuitous with the sex. Doesn't seem to stop violence though. I have no issue with sex, but I care about player comfort levels. So while Exalted is a game where beastiality has game mechanics if it bothers people I'll step in. Same goes for other touchy subjects, rape, torture, child brutality. I do use these lightly because its a brutal setting and the intent is to unnerve you or make you angry. Though if it bothers anyone let me know. It will exist but I can just imply it. I will also always check before I make a player character a victim even if its just implied. While I'm not a fan of plot armor a PC is too close to the actual player for me to risk it.<br /> <br /> In any case if I feel it takes away from the story I'll step in. Typically the less impact it has the more I'll gloss over it. If your character is hedonist that gets laid in every town ok fine but not going into detail about something so common. If sex is the culmination of a relationship built up over a year of real rime I can understand wanting it to be an actual scene to role play. As a GM I will also be graphic if thats the idea. Going to the home of The Lover or house Cynus or a Nexus brothel yea thats part of the setting. Likewise if you go to a Deathlord manse expect me to be detailed about the gore.<br /> <br /> Long story short if its so common it begins to lose narrative weight I'll cut it back.<br /> <br /> 3. Voice chat. Video with that many people gets problematic and my webcam doesn't really work anymore anyways. People also tend to get more self conscious so maybe if the group is comfortable we might switch to video chat. For now, just voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T10:05:37-07:00","id":266268,"title":"","content":"Shall we run character concepts by you?<br /> <br /> And as for rape, sex, and some other sensitive topics, I am one of those who prefers that such things are cut scene'd. It happens, but that doesn't mean we need to roll play through it. And... please don't be too detailed about gore and stuff like that. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T10:52:58-07:00","id":266305,"title":"","content":"I'll try and hit a middle ground of detail and comfort. I do want you guys to be abit bothered by gore, or I should say I wouldn't describe it unless I wanted it to bother your characters, but not ruin the fun. I ask that you tolerate some unease but to inform me if its crossing a line.<br /> <br /> As for running character concept by me and sharing them. Depends. If you want to just post a completed character sheet and I can give my thoughts on it you can. If you dont want to waste time on doing a full write up and rather discuss things as you go feel free to ask me. Really unless its something that would be hard to work in or something really out of the norm the general concept likely wont be an issue. I am betting the backstory and stats meshing are the most likely places there might be an issue. Also a reminder, using errata character creation rules. My philosophy on castes is the intent not the method. You can be an Eclipse caste that negotiates with the point of a sword, or a twilight that uses a network of scholars to research. So even if your character is a master of all fighting styles if he's life is about praising the Unconquered Sun I'd say he's more zenith than dawn.<br /> <br /> On the topic of sharing. I do not require you to publicly post your character sheet. However unless you have reason to hide it I suggest you do so others working on their character can see how the group dynamic is shaping up. <br /> <br /> Oh and please share things you like to see in games. It could be conceptual things, romance, political intrigue, thrilling combat or setting like the wyld or underworld. I'm flexible in what I can do so I'd like to see what you guys would enjoy.<br /> <br /> Finally I want to try one more thing. On a scale of 1-10 with 1 being core book and 10 being mecha-cthullu how much homebrew do you like in your games? I'm curious to see how much players like the GM throwing out of setting stuff at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T11:04:08-07:00","id":266309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266305#post266305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally I want to try one more thing. On a scale of 1-10 with 1 being core book and 10 being mecha-cthullu how much homebrew do you like in your games? I'm curious to see how much players like the GM throwing out of setting stuff at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Wyld, there is nothing ever truly out of setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T11:56:23-07:00","id":266352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266305#post266305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and please share things you like to see in games. It could be conceptual things, romance, political intrigue, thrilling combat or setting like the wyld or underworld. I'm flexible in what I can do so I'd like to see what you guys would enjoy.<br /> <br /> Finally I want to try one more thing. On a scale of 1-10 with 1 being core book and 10 being mecha-cthullu how much homebrew do you like in your games? I'm curious to see how much players like the GM throwing out of setting stuff at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to see a little bit of everything so that a diverse group each have something to contribute and each have places where they're out of their element. Personally I'd like to stick with Creation for the most part as it's generally the most detailed part of the setting. I would prefer to avoid the Wyld (at least to start) so we don't have to pick up charms to not grow extra limbs.<br /> <br /> My experience with homebrew is generally that it's badly designed, thought out and balanced. It also divides between player homebrew and GM homebrew. Player homebrew is about a 2. GM homebrew is about a 9. I find GM's to be interested in providing interesting stories and challenges where players often want to exploit loopholes, but YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T12:04:01-07:00","id":266355,"title":"","content":"I'd say a solid 5 for homebrew, not against or for it. I will always prefer combat over other genres but the only one that I actually dislike is romance.<br /> My favorite setting will always be in Malfeas, but that's probably more for when we can reliably fight a lot of demons(spirits and rogue/bound demons work too).<br /> my character concept is a dusk martial artist(dipping in a utility skill not sure which but leaning towards craft/occult) that's somewhere in the middle of loyalist and rogue.<br /> He was exalted by Black Heron and so has a metric crap ton of freedom compared to other abyssal especially if we're in creation.<br /> <br /> Oh, should we be pre-making chars or wait for everyone to group up to actually put down stat blocks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T13:07:33-07:00","id":266390,"title":"","content":"Just for posterity, game sounds awesome (I've done no stunt mote regen before, it works ok). But there's no way I'd be able to meet a weekly EST game. Good luck and have fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T14:14:17-07:00","id":266430,"title":"","content":"I am also interested in playing, if there is still room. (I'm a lurker on the forum, thus the new account.)<br /> <br /> My favorite games always have a mystery and/or problem solving element to them. Also, enjoy political intrigue and knowing secrets. Not against combat but I would get bored if the combat is &quot;subtract dice rolls until the hit points are zero&quot; type combat.<br /> <br /> I haven't played in a game with home brew, so I am undecided on it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI definitely want to play a Twilight Caste (because Investigation and Lore are awesome), though I'd probably want to discuss a few concepts with you.<br /> <br /> So are we meeting up tonight to discuss stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T16:27:31-07:00","id":266499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266355#post266355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say a solid 5 for homebrew, not against or for it. I will always prefer combat over other genres but the only one that I actually dislike is romance.<br /> My favorite setting will always be in Malfeas, but that's probably more for when we can reliably fight a lot of demons(spirits and rogue/bound demons work too).<br /> my character concept is a dusk martial artist(dipping in a utility skill not sure which but leaning towards craft/occult) that's somewhere in the middle of loyalist and rogue.<br /> He was exalted by Black Heron and so has a metric crap ton of freedom compared to other abyssal especially if we're in creation.<br /> <br /> Oh, should we be pre-making chars or wait for everyone to group up to actually put down stat blocks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok as a heads up I have greatly modified the deathlords, and The Black Heron most of all. In this game she is a &quot;the princess&quot; viewing herself as a woman to be spoiled and pampered. Her motivation is her lost love (whom many wonder if he ever existed). She mutilates people into patchwork monstrosities that she claims is her lover. Eventually this 'thing' fails to fit her unrealistic and constantly shifting view of him. Then violently ripping it apart before creating a new one and denying the last one (or thousands before it) ever existed. If they are lucky they dont survive for long. Her smarter servants know to play along, if her delusion is shaken she does not take it well.<br /> <br /> Though I have no issue with abyssals remember these are heroic characters so hard to be a loyalist, gonna have to give me a justification as to why he'd work with them and why they would let him join at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266430#post266430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not against combat but I would get bored if the combat is &quot;subtract dice rolls until the hit points are zero&quot; type combat.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> So are we meeting up tonight to discuss stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div>Than you will enjoy my combat because you wont do well at mid-late game if your solution is to poke the enemy till it dies. Not unless you are prepared to lose alot.<br /> <br /> And well I'm on skype tonight if you guys want to message me or discuss things. Its aerozord<br /> but not really anything vital, so dont feel you have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:09:52-07:00","id":266516,"title":"","content":"Could you pm me your changes to the death lords. The undecided shtick for loyalties was really more for drama if its just a wrench for the story I can trivially drop it. Think Zuko from avatar he just wants to be accepted for what he is now and both groups give and take from that need.<br /> p.s. there's two Aerozords are you in the one in Youngtown or just flat united states","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T17:12:35-07:00","id":266517,"title":"","content":"go with youngstown one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:09:04-07:00","id":266538,"title":"","content":"Sent you my character concept via PM. Let me know if I need to adjust anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T10:35:35-07:00","id":266850,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I was thinking of starting the game in the North. I actually dont know a whole lot about it, but thought it might be a nice change since its rarely used. Give you guys an environment you need to worry about. Please dont take that to mean you need to load up on survival charms, in fact dont do that because it kind of defeats the purpose when you can run around a blizzard naked with no ill effects.<br /> <br /> Anyways thats just an idea I wanted opinions on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T11:17:35-07:00","id":266880,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about the North myself, but I'm fine with it. The only two areas that I'd be not to happy to play in is the Blessed Isle (I feel that the Blessed Isle is sort of end game area for solars) and the West (I already played in the West).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T12:07:18-07:00","id":266932,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with the North as well.<br /> <br /> Will we be using the full Exalted 2.5 errata? I have PM'd you a first draft character sheet. <br /> <br /> For those that are looking to join the game as well, I have created a Night caste Solar who is a Thief, Partier and Womanizer and is focused on sneaking and stealing. I'll post the sheet after it's been through the ringer with Aeroz. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The changes to the Deathlords sound fine to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T12:14:39-07:00","id":266937,"title":"","content":"Awesome! My Scavenger Lord Twilight needs a Partner in Crime for all the artifacts and ancient tomes she's going to &quot;rescue&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T12:29:23-07:00","id":266950,"title":"","content":"Tis a dark day indeed when the abyssal is the conscience of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:04:22-07:00","id":266994,"title":"","content":"Ha! I saw you were playing an Abyssal and realized that there might be a bit of inter-PC conflict with her &quot;Tomb Raider&quot; past. Because those ghosts don't need all those first age artifacts; they should be in Lethe anyways. *ducks*<br /> <br /> (My character has high compassion, so it should be really easy to convince her not to steal from ghosts.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:15:12-07:00","id":267001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=266950#post266950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tis a dark day indeed when the abyssal is the conscience of the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>My wife is wondering why I'm laughing out loud. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T14:39:13-07:00","id":267017,"title":"","content":"crap guys I just realized we didn't discuss what to do about languages.<br /> <br /> I also think I'll house rule that each dot gives you a new language and that number dialects. So it works like this<br /> 0- native language<br /> 1- one extra language and one dialect<br /> 2- two extra languages and three dialects<br /> 3- three extra languages and six dialects<br /> ........<br /> <br /> low/high realm will be considered dialects of each other. So you can take one as a language and another as a dialect. Same with old realm and autocthian. Sound good to people? Hope this will help with getting everyone to be able to communicate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T15:10:42-07:00","id":267028,"title":"","content":"oh crap languages are actually a thing this game thanks for reminding me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T16:31:32-07:00","id":267045,"title":"","content":"Is there a list of dialects somewhere?<br /> <br /> Also, my character has Riverspeak, Skytongue, and Old Realm for languages. I can pick up one of the other Realm languages if needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T16:39:50-07:00","id":267049,"title":"","content":"I've gone with Riverspeak and Skytongue (tentatively)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:04:56-07:00","id":267793,"title":"","content":"I was looking over the archery charms again and need some advice. I originally took 'There is no wind' and 'forceful arrow'. Should I switch them out for 'Essence Arrow Technique' and 'Phantom Arrow'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:27:13-07:00","id":267798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=267793#post267793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking over the archery charms again and need some advice. I originally took 'There is no wind' and 'forceful arrow'. Should I switch them out for 'Essence Arrow Technique' and 'Phantom Arrow'?</div> </div> </div> </div>depends on your playstyle honestly. Are you more concerned with always having your weapon or with always hitting your target","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:21:36-07:00","id":267859,"title":"","content":"Probably with always hitting your target, at least at first. Do you expect there will be situations where my character will not be able to bring her weapon with her?<br /> <br /> I tweaked my character and now have Archery 5 and There is No Wind and Accuracy Without Distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-28-2014, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T22:37:09-07:00","id":268004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=267859#post267859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably with always hitting your target, at least at first. Do you expect there will be situations where my character will not be able to bring her weapon with her?<br /> <br /> I tweaked my character and now have Archery 5 and There is No Wind and Accuracy Without Distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, or at the very least unable to openly carry it. Captured, weapon is gone. At a dinner party, weapon is gone. Disarming attack, weapon is gone. There are alot of reasons for this to happen. However I mean this situation is possible, not that it will happen any time soon and honestly it depends alot on you guys and how you approach situations. Of course this isn't always a problem either. Someone could disarm you just to try and diffuse a situation and end a fight for example. I'm not saying this to discourage your choice, just keep yourself aware of the trade off so you can think up other ways to compensate. <br /> <br /> That does remind me. Guys include equipment that you can buy at your resource level. Basically whatever you want that (resource level -1) and I will allow one item at your resource level. Remember your character will have to carry the stuff so dont do what one player did and start the game with 500 knives. We will also be in the North so, a coat would be a good idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T06:31:36-07:00","id":268216,"title":"","content":"I'll probably pick up the &quot;always have the weapon&quot; charms eventually. I don't expect that we will be getting invites to dinner parties any time soon. And hopefully, everyone will be distracted by the big abyssal standing in front of my character to think of disarming little old me.<br /> <br /> I found a <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkb1dVSjBvWHpHX3M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">picture</a> of what my character looks like. The yellow and sunset orange color scheme fits what her anima banner too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 09-29-2014, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T08:28:17-07:00","id":268274,"title":"","content":"How does craft interact with the resources limit? I'm effectively craft 5 for armor smithing (specialties) and made articulated plate while under the silver prince(changed my Deathlord though pm conversation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:05:45-07:00","id":268320,"title":"","content":"Its still going off your resource limit, you can craft stuff in game but it will have to be in game. I know that doesn't make alot of in character sense but I'm making that ruling for balance reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:26:30-07:00","id":268329,"title":"","content":"Back to the character sheet *grumble grumble* this is why I use interactive character sheets so editing isn't as much a pain.<br /> <br /> huh, that only took like 5min. just switched out the two charms for eternally wearing armor to iron kettle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","user":"Eura","date":". 09-29-2014, 01:53 PM"},