content":"I'm sorry Mayu killed Limp, Spaace. I know you wanted a pet wyld thing. ;-) <br /> <br /> I don't think I've ever been so excited about sleep in a role playing game before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T05:57:18-07:00","id":293663,"title":"","content":"Since we have been talking about dice rollers: <a href=\"http://catchyourhare.com/diceroller/\" target=\"_blank\">http://catchyourhare.com/diceroller/</a><br /> <br /> At the very least, I would like to use a dice roller for combat. It is quite obvious when a combat roll fails (you miss!). I think this will give us a happy compromise between not knowing that we failed a perception check and the joy of rolling a whole crap ton of dice. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 10-27-2014, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:18:34-07:00","id":293683,"title":"","content":"That one looks better than the one we were using. It capped out at 10d10 which made it a pain when you had to roll 14 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T06:58:49-07:00","id":293703,"title":"","content":"Do we integrate the Infernal into our group yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:50:37-07:00","id":294223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=293703#post293703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we integrate the Infernal into our group yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>After talking with the others I decided to disallow infernals. Ultimately removing infernals as a setting element because I feel as a storyteller I can give you guys a more interesting storyhook with those 50 solar shards having another purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T07:42:58-07:00","id":297103,"title":"","content":"just a reminder, tomorrow we will be starting alittle after 9pm EST. Again sorry about the delay, new job, odd hours","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:01:40-07:00","id":297117,"title":"","content":"That's ok. It's Halloween after all and that leaves more time to give out candy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T08:09:24-07:00","id":297123,"title":"","content":"I'm cursed. Whenever I buy candy to give out, no one shows up. When I don't buy candy, I end up digging in my cupboard for hot chocolate or something to give the two kids that show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T11:40:49-07:00","id":297284,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't you get candy?! Eat the leftovers for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T11:44:55-07:00","id":297287,"title":"","content":"I'm not much of a candy person. I usually buy a bag of snickers, eat it too fast, and then feel sick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T21:05:50-07:00","id":298659,"title":"","content":"The dice roller: <a href=\"https://rolz.org/group\" target=\"_blank\">https://rolz.org/group</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T12:31:40-07:00","id":299184,"title":"","content":"good news and bad news, bad news is my work schedule is the same for next week, good news is thats as bad as it will be. Just be ready to jump in when I get home<br /> <br /> Oh and everyone please post your current character sheets, I'll modify the first post with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T13:08:34-07:00","id":299208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit\" target=\"_blank\"> http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also was working on a few custom charms when I get bored. Figured I'd post the rough draft of them<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Death's Grip (seriously why isnt this canon)<br /> Cost: 3m or 3m, 1Wp Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive (Step 1)<br /> Keywords: Combo-Ok, Obvious, War<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Owl Seizes Mouse<br /> Pulls target into melee range from essence x 10 yards by making a Strength or Dexterity + Martial Arts roll with essence bonus successes against their DV.<br /> For the extra cost of a willpower this can be used in mass combat against a unit of essence magnitude or less. Death's grip can be used in tandem with a<br /> blockade action forgoing the blockade roll so long as the target is successfully pulled. Death's grip can only be used once per turn so while 3 people<br /> can be blockaded only one can be enhanced with this charm.<br /> <br /> Notes: Not sure if I should add war as a minimum trait or how mass combat formations deal with a mass pull.<br /> <br /> Reap The flesh<br /> Cost: 2m Mins: athletics 3, essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive (Step 10)<br /> Keywords: Combo-Ok<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Corpse-surge Might<br /> The deathknight pull an enormous surge of might as his weapon sinks into his victim's flesh making all 10's on the damage roll count as two successes.<br /> This charm can explicitly be used with other abilities.<br /> <br /> Notes: I'm debating if Reap the Flesh really needs a prerequisite charm or if an athletics excellency is better.<br /> <br /> Naught but a sound<br /> cost:- Mins: Martial arts 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Emotion, compulsion<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dark Messiah Form<br /> The screams of the living grow irksome after a while, and so an irritated deathknight created this charm just to silence the monologing dragon-blooded.<br /> When Dark Messiah Form is active if the Deathknight designates all of his attacks confered by the form against one target they cannot speak or create<br /> sound of any kind for an action unless aided by magic this can be ignored for a willpower. If silenced for more actions than their conviction they gain an<br /> intimacy of dread against the deathknight.<br /> <br /> Notes: While a bit meh in power you'd be amazed how often you talk in a narrative fight. Would having high MDV to resist the silence effect hurt the<br /> charm too much? It might be more thematic/funny to make such a resistance mechanic use parry MDV. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T17:07:53-07:00","id":299480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T17:21:22-08:00","id":300560,"title":"","content":"Ok added mayu and bloodless's profiles, I also included some NPCs. I'm doing those as an example. I'd prefer you guys making up the profiles from your characters perspective so you can include conjecture. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=299208#post299208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNb21NdjUzV0JsdlE/edit\" target=\"_blank\">http://docs.google.com/file/d/0B_bGa...UzV0JsdlE/edit</a><br /> <br /> I also was working on a few custom charms when I get bored. Figured I'd post the rough draft of them<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Death's Grip (seriously why isnt this canon)<br /> Cost: 3m or 3m, 1Wp Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 3<br /> Type: Reflexive (Step 1)<br /> Keywords: Combo-Ok, Obvious, War<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Owl Seizes Mouse<br /> Pulls target into melee range from essence x 10 yards by making a Strength or Dexterity + Martial Arts roll with essence bonus successes against their DV.<br /> For the extra cost of a willpower this can be used in mass combat against a unit of essence magnitude or less. Death's grip can be used in tandem with a<br /> blockade action forgoing the blockade roll so long as the target is successfully pulled. Death's grip can only be used once per turn so while 3 people<br /> can be blockaded only one can be enhanced with this charm.<br /> <br /> Notes: Not sure if I should add war as a minimum trait or how mass combat formations deal with a mass pull.<br /> <br /> Reap The flesh<br /> Cost: 2m Mins: athletics 3, essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive (Step 10)<br /> Keywords: Combo-Ok<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Corpse-surge Might<br /> The deathknight pull an enormous surge of might as his weapon sinks into his victim's flesh making all 10's on the damage roll count as two successes.<br /> This charm can explicitly be used with other abilities.<br /> <br /> Notes: I'm debating if Reap the Flesh really needs a prerequisite charm or if an athletics excellency is better.<br /> <br /> Naught but a sound<br /> cost:- Mins: Martial arts 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: Emotion, compulsion<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dark Messiah Form<br /> The screams of the living grow irksome after a while, and so an irritated deathknight created this charm just to silence the monologing dragon-blooded.<br /> When Dark Messiah Form is active if the Deathknight designates all of his attacks confered by the form against one target they cannot speak or create<br /> sound of any kind for an action unless aided by magic this can be ignored for a willpower. If silenced for more actions than their conviction they gain an<br /> intimacy of dread against the deathknight.<br /> <br /> Notes: While a bit meh in power you'd be amazed how often you talk in a narrative fight. Would having high MDV to resist the silence effect hurt the<br /> charm too much? It might be more thematic/funny to make such a resistance mechanic use parry MDV. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok lets take a look.<br /> Death's Grip. I get the idea is to bring the other guy into melee range instead of you using owl seizes mouse to go to them. I think it should be a simple combo-basic charm since charms that affect battle positions are incredibly powerful. Drop the bonus successes too. Mass combat aspect, not sure of as I doubt we'll be using mass combat as written in the book.<br /> <br /> Reap the Flesh: Definitely a supplemental charm. I know there are charms similar to this so I'd have to check them for cost comparison. I think the prereq is good though<br /> <br /> Naught but a Sound: This I dislike for narrative reasons. Its hard enough to get good banter, and taunting in a fight without you having a permanent charm designed specifically to negate it. If you as a player dislike a NPC monologing than let me know and I'll work around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T22:40:18-08:00","id":300772,"title":"","content":"I mainly just made &quot;naught but a sound&quot; because I liked the charm name and jotted it down just in case I wanted to use it as a ST in my local group. I've also grown to associate big bad evil guy/arrogant pc monologue as mental masturbation. It's just so rarely done well and EVERYONE think's the're (screw you constantly changing grammar rules) the one that did it well. That being said Arthas' monologues are amazing.<br /> <br /> Supplemental for &quot;reap the flesh&quot; is fine, I'm just saying there are a fair amount of abyssal &quot;wound shenanigans&quot; charms that are activated at step 10.<br /> <br /> Death's grip was originally a contested roll, guess I forgot to take out the bonus successes. The whole simple thing hurts my idea of the pull/lariat combo. If it's simple I'd like it to be speed 4-5 and debatably dv- 0 although -1 is ok. The thing is Death's grip has 6 charms before it with owl seizes mouse being extremely potent I'm worried it might go &quot;I could pull him but the charge is so much less situational.&quot; If I'm going to be gambling experience on super situational charms I'd rather stack ox-bodies and make some poor dragon-blooded(diplomat of course) spend an hour beating me to death. If mass combat is a little more Hodge podge It can always work like peony blossom with one roll against a myriad of DV's.<br /> <br /> As a point of clarification I mean situational by &quot;how often am I going to use this in a fight?&quot; as resorting to using combat tactics can be seen as situational compared to social tactics which can be used for everything if you have the whit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T00:02:49-08:00","id":300812,"title":"","content":"It wont be as directly effective as owl seizes mouse for a very good reason. Owl seizes mouse has you going to where they are as opposed to them going to you. Typically both parties will try to position themselves in an advantageous location. The other guy controls where this grapple will take place which discourages spamming it. The reverse however gives you a HUGE advantage. You can pull him away from support, into striking range of your allies, into a hazardous environment you are immune to but he is not. Thats just off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T00:45:58-08:00","id":300849,"title":"","content":"I may have put more emphasis on my weariness of death's grasp being a flash in the pan than I thought, I blame it on being late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T17:27:19-08:00","id":301585,"title":"","content":"Alric's current character sheet:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_kLDAvk555U1FBbklHYVgtN1k/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Hey, we got bumped to the &quot;Conventions and Gatherings&quot; subforum...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","user":"Spaaace","date":".  Bumped 11-04-2014, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T10:00:25-08:00","id":303369,"title":"","content":"Aeroz, did you want to change the title of the post to include that it is an Exalted game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/