rive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T08:05:31-08:00","id":339048,"title":"","content":"Bloodless - Did you needa any help getting custom charms into Anathema? I might be able to help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:03:04-08:00","id":339264,"title":"","content":"It'd be nice yes, give me a second to write the revised version of my charms<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> Death's Grip (seriously why isnt this canon)<br /> Cost: 3m or 3m, 1Wp Mins: Martial Arts 4, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple (speed 5)<br /> Keywords: Combo-simple, Obvious, War<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Owl Seizes Mouse<br /> Pulls target into melee range from essence x 10 yards by making a Strength or Dexterity + Martial Arts roll against their DV.<br /> For the extra cost of a willpower this can be used in mass combat against a unit of essence magnitude or less. In non-mass combat scenarios the abyssal can make one roll against a number of targets equal to his essence*8. Death's grip can be used in tandem with a blockade action forgoing the blockade roll so long as the target is successfully pulled. Death's grip can only be used once per turn so while 3 people can be blockaded only one can be enhanced with this charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Reap The flesh<br /> Cost: 2m Mins: athletics 3, essence 2<br /> Type: supplemental<br /> Keywords: Combo-Ok<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Corpse-surge Might<br /> The deathknight pull an enormous surge of might as his weapon sinks into his victim's flesh making all 10's on the damage roll count as two successes.<br /> This charm can explicitly be used with other abilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","user":"Eura","date":".  cherms 12-13-2014, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:12:03-08:00","id":339524,"title":"","content":"Hey. The custom charms are added via XML. I'll play around with it and see what I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:18:04-08:00","id":339530,"title":"","content":"Its also good to figure out in general when you guys eventually make custom charms. Custom charms really flesh out a game in so many ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:53:25-08:00","id":339544,"title":"","content":"So... I got Anathema to run without error with test charm, but it won't show up on the charm tree. I'll give it a try later. <br /> <br /> Here is what I have so far: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkOWdBSnNTZEV0Z1k&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...1k&amp;usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:35:04-08:00","id":339630,"title":"","content":"Ok. So I got the charms to show up. Death's Grip isn't showing up under Martial Arts for some reason, but under charms (it created a new group for Dark Messiah under charms). <br /> <br /> I'll keep working on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:45:17-08:00","id":339636,"title":"","content":"I've got it working: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_kLDAvk555RnIwbUNEZWpsZGc/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bw_...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> You will need to unzip these files into your &lt;Install Path&gt;\\Anathema\\repository\\custom folder and restart the application. You will see Reap The Flesh embedded in the Athletics charms, but since Death's Grip is a custom MA charm, it has a new category under the Abyssal selection. It's not actually part of the Martial Art, but an extension which I guess is Abyssal specific. Under Charm Type, pick Abyssal and under Charm Group, pick (Celestial) Dark Messiah Style<br /> <br /> One thing is that there doesn't seem to be a Combo-Simple keyword (as per Death's Grip) so I've left that off. Please check it over to make sure it's correct. I don't know enough about making charms to be sure that it's correct in all respects.<br /> <br /> Let me know how it works.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't update before uploading, so it looks like you have your choice of implementations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","user":"Spaaace","date":". 12-13-2014, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:53:41-08:00","id":339641,"title":"","content":"Got it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkOWdBSnNTZEV0Z1k&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkOWdBSnNTZEV0Z1k&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkOWdBSnNTZEV0Z1k&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0B-UiWxItb8fkOWdBSnNTZEV0Z1k&amp;usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Copy the three files from the custom folder I linked into &lt;Anathema Install Location&gt;\\Anathema\\repository\\custom<br /> <br /> The location of the Owl Seizes Mouse and Death's Grip will different (it will not be on the end of the row anymore).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-13-2014, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:54:11-08:00","id":339642,"title":"","content":"You have to create a separate file for Martial Arts charms (with the Charms_MartialArts_SecondEdition_BloodlessMA file name). I found that out the hard way. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:03:10-08:00","id":339647,"title":"","content":"Be sure to check the opening post to make sure your info is correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:07:25-08:00","id":339651,"title":"","content":"I updated my character sheet file on Google Drive.<br /> <br /> Anywho, my XP goals for Mayu is to get to Craft 4, the first Craft Excellency, and Craftsman Needs No Tools. Then to save up for Essence 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-13-2014, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:35:08-08:00","id":339690,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_bGakUT9OwNbWhIYjZPZHp3MjA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_b...ew?usp=sharing</a> for updated Bloodless<br /> I'm just going to pretend I understood how to do all that jazz. I'm sure it looks harder than it really is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:39:54-08:00","id":341936,"title":"","content":"I would like to clarify the custom charm Bloodless made: from the main 2e book it says that supernatural martial arts are complete and can't be expanded. I assume that Bloodless's charm is like the Solar Martial Arts charms which chain off the Solar Hero Style, but aren't actually part of the style. Is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:59:34-08:00","id":341947,"title":"","content":"Based on what I saw in Anathema, that is most likely correct. Owl Seizes Mouse seems to be an Abyssal only charm. A Solar who knows Dark Messiah Style doesn't have access to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 12-16-2014, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T09:50:44-08:00","id":342029,"title":"","content":"All hero styles have expansions charms that only that specific exalt can learn. The sad thing is lunar hero style has pretty good expansion charms but the core stuff is so terrible nobody will ever take them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:06:04-08:00","id":342425,"title":"","content":"Just chiming in as ST, you can expand on the hero style but it counts as a native charm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T18:55:26-08:00","id":342475,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks.<br /> <br /> As for this Friday, I'm around any time after 8:30 (solo parenting again).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T07:12:50-08:00","id":343861,"title":"","content":"So, I have been looking around at custom charms others have written. These looks interesting: <br /> <br /> Archery:<br /> <br /> <b>Unerring Memorial Arrow</b><br /> Having tested her accuracy against her target once, the Solar's aim becomes truer. After the Solar makes a successful attack against a target and deals damage, the Solar may repeat that exact attack during her next action, using the same charms, gambits, techniques and merits. All dice that come up as a 9 when rolling to attack count as two successes. The Solar can repeat the attack again to make 8s and 7s count as two successes as well. However, the Solar's successes on the attack and damage rolls cannot exceed the successes of the original attack being copied.<br /> <br /> <b>Broken Arrow</b><br /> The Solar supports her allies with her archery. This charm supports an attack against an enemy who is engaged in close-range combat against one of the Solar's allies and possesses a momentum advantage over that ally. If the attack is successful, the Solar's ally can immediately take a movement action to escape, even if it would normally be impossible for her to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Craft:<br /> <br /> <b>Gracious Fellowship Bequeathal</b><br /> <i>The Solar's passion drives his artifice. When rolling to craft an object specifically for someone towards whom the Solar holds a positive Minor Tie, the Solar counts 9s as two successes. If the Intimacy is a positive Major Tie, 8s count as two successes as well and if the Intimacy is a positive Defining Tie, 7s also count as two successes.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Lore:<br /> <br /> <b>Omniscient Index Technique</b><br /> When the Solar does not know something, either because she failed a Lore roll or the knowledge is simply beyond her scope, she at least knows which references to consult for information.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Awareness:<br /> <br /> <b>Wind Stalker's Instinct</b><br /> This charm allows the Solar to take aim actions against a target whom she knows is present, even if they are currently hidden. The Solar's first attack against the target gains the benefits of aiming. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.co