ontent":"A brief summary of the evening for Bloodless and Baldur. Aero and Mayu, please feel to jump in or correct me where appropriate.<br /> <br /> We set off on our journey to the Factory-Cathedral and arrived at an exhaust port(?) without incident after about a day. We decided to leave Baldur/Bloodless to set up camp while Mayu and Alric went exploring. Mayu can't climb, so had to be tied to a rope and lowered down by Makoto. Alric threw a handful of snow into the hole and gracefully stepped from flake to flake on the way down. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The tunnels were coated with ice and we found a bio-engineered critter that wasn't aggressive, burrowing through the ice with some kind of acidic vomit. We didn't push our luck and he didn't attack, so we left him alone. He seemed to recognize/acknowledge us when we got it's attention, but again, not aggressive. <br /> <br /> The city itself looks like it was grown or bio-engineered in its entirety. The buildings are unique, and very tall. The streets are lit by glowbugs in cases. The streets are kept clean by small critters that pop out and pick up anything littered almost as soon as it hits the ground. Looks like there isn't anyone there; no bodies or traces of any people we could see.<br /> <br /> In the middle was a fountain of vaguely greenish goo and a Manse. We tried going in, but security didn't like Alric. Probably thought he would steal something (and they would be right). It seemed to recognize Mayu's Exaltation and allowed her limited access. When she went into the Hearthroom (ignoring the &quot;Keep Out&quot; sign), there was a giant queen ant/birthing thorax monster with Soulsteel jaws and the hearthstone embedded in it's brow. It wasn't happy about Mayu being there, so she retreated. <br /> <br /> That's about all we got to for the evening. Next up is figuring out how to get control of the Manse without dying or wrecking it.<br /> <br /> It was a fun evening of the Alric/Mayu odd couple of &quot;You go ahead Mayu; I'll be right behind you. Promise.&quot; Good times!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:16:16-08:00","id":359101,"title":"","content":"A few things:<br /> <br /> 1) There is something odd about the Essence flow in the Hearthstone room. The hearthstone room is usually saturated with Essence, but this one seems to drained of it.<br /> 2) The Queen seems to eat magical materials. We saw one of her workers feed her a small sliver of Orichalcum.<br /> 3) Security seems to be very non aggressive. The guard creatures did not pursue Alric as soon as he left the area he didn't have security access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:41:56-08:00","id":359562,"title":"","content":"So did Baldur fall off the face of the earth or just extenuating circumstances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/