eonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T13:59:49-08:00","id":364756,"title":"","content":"we'll figure something out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T01:45:31-08:00","id":365211,"title":"","content":"So I figured out my first artifact project, It's combining the smash fists and the bioklaive into something akin to a soul steel <a href=\"http://th07.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2014/301/a/c/kargath_bladefist_by_daerone-d84foa2.png\" target=\"_blank\">http://th07.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/...ne-d84foa2.png</a><br /> The bioklaive would take on a more armored scorpion appearance, gain the martial artist and clinch tag, take on the stats of either a reaper daiklaive with a minor bonus in damage or a reaver daiklaive depending on how its tail forms(It's not interchangeable once its made so it's set in stone), and the real thing that makes this combo a unique artifact is that it counts both as a gauntlet and/or daiklaive whenever its convenient.<br /> <br /> Notes: It's probably artifact 3 or a high end artifact 2, either way that's magic tech 4+ and the main reason I want to make this is because I can't use my martial arts charms with the bioklaive.<br /> Also I get to play with sword based martial arts so the infamous even blade style would be an option or if I'm stupid lucky violet bier of sorrows ( yes I realize its a severity 4 offense to teach a non-sidereal that style).<br /> <br /> I just prefer to get custom things pre-approved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T13:29:10-08:00","id":365710,"title":"","content":"Ok, the general idea is not bad, specific stats and whatnot aside, and need to work out from a narrative standpoint how it physically works but thats not too hard. However the bioklave is not magitech, its craft genesis. The magic material outer edge is just a shell, its a living thing.<br /> <br /> This didn't come up in story but I think I should tell you it has a &quot;sheathed&quot; state. It turns itself on your arm and retracts a portion of the tail into itself. That way you can still have it attached and use your hands. Now you cant rapidly switch between the two so you might still aim for your idea, just letting you know. For future reference, making new life with craft genesis will get some resonance but just modifying it wouldn't. There is also the more morbid option of using necrotech, killing it and using its corpse as the foundation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:17:24-08:00","id":365743,"title":"","content":"I was actually considering taking Craft Genesis instead of Craft Magitech (since the Manse is Genesis based). Mayu doesn't have any medicine yet, but it is a Caste Ability. We probably need someone that knows some Medicine anyways.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know there is a lot of stuff I'd like to spend XP on for Mayu. I'll need to make a decision eventually on what to focus on. )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-10-2015, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:48:20-08:00","id":365856,"title":"","content":"And for my part, I will be focusing on Night caste like things and probably some combat upgrades. I think I might pick up something to resist social influence, but rely on mundane means to effect social results; theft, blackmail. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T20:33:12-08:00","id":365972,"title":"","content":"I'm just trying to figure out ways I'd use the bioklaive as more than an excuse to learn melee charms. I'm assuming the sheathed mode isn't conspicuous so the elsewhere charm isn't near mandatory. I suppose if I get arise and slaughter and used a melee weapon it'd help my war ghost bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T21:52:16-08:00","id":366045,"title":"","content":"abit more ooc info. Since its a living thing when those few that did try them out tended to get rather attached so they didn't store them in elsewhere. They were designed to be with the exalt at most times. It kind of needs you to live outside the nutrient and essence filled nursery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T11:45:35-08:00","id":367611,"title":"","content":"After getting all the Craft stuff, I am going to hold off on upping Mayu's Essence and focus on more Archery Charms or getting Athletics. Might pick up Leaping Dodge Method.<br /> <br /> Then I will focus on Lore/Linguistics Charms. Mostly because after finding the city, her motivation will shift and she is going to be focused on increasing the standard of living for the North. She was already pretty shocked about how people lived in the North to begin with, but after finding a first age city, it's going to be more of a drive to her. Mayu knows she can't do it all on her own, so she is going to start with increasing the education of the area.<br /> <br /> This is going to be a pretty long term goal, thus the investment in combat charms. She has to survive to see this happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-12-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T00:01:14-08:00","id":368360,"title":"","content":"The real question is will the ST keep the 1xp surcharge for changing a non-completed motivation. I suppose I could help in this endeavor with war charms but those make the targets sociopaths, I'll consider that branch when we actually have an empire. The next few sessions will decide if I go necromancy, melee, or something weird like sagacious reading of intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:12:22-08:00","id":368590,"title":"","content":"I don't think we'll need to build an empire. I was thinking more setting up a system of learning at first and then set up workshops that sell upgraded technology. But, if the rest of the group wants to build an empire, Mayu could be convince that this is the best way to achieve her goal.<br /> <br /> At lore 5, she probably has discovered a lot of lost lore from the first age, including a whole city! I'm not sure if that counts and completing her motivation or not. (Might have to break into that library) I feel like it is more of an evolution of her motivations. She has discovered lost lore, now she wants to share it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:04:21-08:00","id":368620,"title":"","content":"At minimum its going to cause nations to rise, too much of a game changer for it not to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:47:24-08:00","id":368670,"title":"","content":"I'm sure they will rise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mayu hasn't really thought though the political implications of what she wants to do. For one thing, I'm sure Lookshy (and by extension her brother) would LOVE to have a competing civilization that runs on near first age technology. /sarcasm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:33:04-08:00","id":368694,"title":"","content":"There's only room for one Makoto in this world. Bro has go to go! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:35:35-08:00","id":368698,"title":"","content":"Noooo!!!! My background points!!!! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:21:58-08:00","id":368721,"title":"","content":"Free factory cathedral and Manse.<br /> <br /> /drop_mic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:25:34-08:00","id":368724,"title":"","content":"I seriously doubt there aren't strings attached things have gone too smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:28:42-08:00","id":368728,"title":"","content":"Well, sure. I'm sure there will be some punching involved, either now to take it or later to keep it.<br /> <br /> Makoto can die heroically setting up his sister's empire. See? Everyone wins! =D<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","user":"Spaaace","date":". 01-13-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:53:36-08:00","id":368741,"title":"","content":"Every time you say Makoto I'm just imagining the polar bear dog being an exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:54:38-08:00","id":368744,"title":"","content":"Yes. Instead of Makoto secretly being a Sidereal, he is secretly a lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:57:50-08:00","id":368747,"title":"","content":"The Polar Bear Dog is an Urcanis. Or is it Ur-Canis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T11:01:46-08:00","id":368750,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure which is the correct spelling. Aeroz?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:50:53-08:00","id":369278,"title":"","content":"So, now that Alric is Essence 3, I was considering Infinite Melee Mastery as a quick way to get better results in combat. I'm fighting with two weapons anways, so adding 6 dice to every attack for free seems like a really good deal. Other than the 1wp part of the cost, is there some downside that I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T00:05:00-08:00","id":369533,"title":"","content":"Well it's a simple charm with no keywords so every time you activate the charm you're going to be vulnerable, It's also going to eat a good chunk out of your personal essence so you're paying for what you get. Other than that infinite mastery is very powerful. The big reason I'm not getting it is because I already have a massive mote commitment with my soak and form charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T04:47:50-08:00","id":369667,"title":"","content":"I see what you are saying about the Simple keyword, but it is Scene length, so the six motes you put in return three dice for every melee action. After the first two attacks, it has paid for itself and you're getting 'free' motes after that.<br /> <br /> I misread the charm though; you get a price reduction for every two motes, so only three dice on every attack, but that is still awesome. I just need to find space in combat to make time to activate it. Between you creating a distraction and Stealth, I should be able to find the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T05:17:15-08:00","id":369676,"title":"","content":"Having a high join battle pool also really helps in such matters, it's a stat that's often forgotten about and can allow you to get a cheeky simple charm off with little consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:01:25-08:00","id":370159,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if it was clear or not, but the big advantage of the factory cathedral is it can make any type of bioklaive. Meaning with the resources you can quickly arm any and all exalted. Beyond that this isn't a city with near first age tech its one WITH first age tech. Technology that was considered the bleeding edge of living artifacts even then. As proof by the fact its still running. Oh but why wasn't it sacked like most other first age cities? Mystery mystery<br /> <br /> As a reminder, factory cathedrals require sacrifices to keep running unlike most manses which are self-sustaining. The answer is something boring but I'm hoping it will lead to more fun quests afterwards. Assuming I dont change it on a whim because I thought of something better. I suspect it will be awhile before you guys are ready to get this up and running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:10:00-08:00","id":370170,"title":"","content":"How many meat cows are there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:13:09-08:00","id":370273,"title":"","content":"You saw two there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:20:14-08:00","id":371055,"title":"","content":"I have some questions about the city:<br /> <br /> 1. Is it an actual city sized place or something more like an estate?<br /> 2. Is the manse the same thing as the factory-cathedral, or are they separate things (even though the Queen seems to live in the Manse)?<br /> 3. Is it typical that a circle all attune to a Manse as a group binding or other show of mutual ownership or is it typically 1-1 Manse-Exalt?<br /> <br /> Probably more questions based on the answers.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T10:23:49-08:00","id":371211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=371055#post371055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some questions about the city:<br /> <br /> 1. Is it an actual city sized place or something more like an estate?<br /> Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an actual city<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=371055#post371055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Is the manse the same thing as the factory-cathedral, or are they separate things (even though the Queen seems to live in the Manse)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't actually a manse, it was just a building you originally mistook for a manse. the queen IS the manse/factory cathedral<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=371055#post371055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Is it typical that a circle all attune to a Manse as a group binding or other show of mutual ownership or is it typically 1-1 Manse-Exalt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically one person can attune to a manse (though there are some specifically designed to break this rule), but attunement isn't the same as ownership. Multiple people can be given equal access to the manse systems. Do remember this one is very unique. This manse is a living thing, its also unclear just how connected it is to the surrounding systems. Which might function completely independent of the queen or only some are directly influenced","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:07:12-08:00","id":372781,"title":"","content":"We starting at 8:30 EST tonight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:35:04-08:00","id":372800,"title":"","content":"8 or 8:30 depending on player situations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:08:47-08:00","id":373292,"title":"","content":"Updated Character Sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkVGNJdHN5TV91bG8/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:15:52-08:00","id":373294,"title":"","content":"So I was looking at Athletics Charms. There is one called Increasing Strength Exercise. Would this be a better charm to buy instead of Thunderbolt Attack Prana for increasing Archery damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:57:03-08:00","id":373312,"title":"","content":"If you have an artifact weapon to negate the maximum strength rating increasing strength exercise will give better sustain damage. Thunderbolt attack prana gives way better burst but costs willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:59:48-08:00","id":373313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=373294#post373294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was looking at Athletics Charms. There is one called Increasing Strength Exercise. Would this be a better charm to buy instead of Thunderbolt Attack Prana for increasing Archery damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>strictly for attack damage increase, no. For one non-artifact bows have an upper limit on the strength you can apply to their damage. and thuderbolt can deal more raw damage anyways.<br /> <br /> However thats not to say strength increasing exercise doesn't have its uses, its scene length and increases your strength for all rolls. But its a general use charm where thunderbolt attack prana is specifically a damage booster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T07:29:16-08:00","id":373454,"title":"","content":"What would I need to do to create an Artifact long bow? Would that fall under Craft Mundane or Craft Magitech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T08:43:07-08:00","id":373498,"title":"","content":"You can technically use both but magitech gives far less penalties. Unfortunately magitech is also a total pain in the ass to get to any good level. What's worse is that power bows are at least artifact two and the longbow is artifact 3 so it's also time/material consuming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T08:58:00-08:00","id":373509,"title":"","content":"I already have the prereqs to get Magictech to Level 4 (I have Craft Mundane 4 and Lore 5). I can also get Craft Genesis to Level 2 (Lore 5, Occult 4, Medicine 2). Maybe it would be easier to Grow my own bow with Craft Genesis than build it with Craft Magitech.<br /> <br /> Though I don't want to step on Bloodless' crafting niche. He was focusing on weapons and armor, correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-17-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T09:40:29-08:00","id":373558,"title":"","content":"yes but two exalts using craft charms together gives a metric crap ton of bonus dice/successes, so on the bigger artifact projects the help is appreciated. I still need to work on my lore and occult before I can have enough magitech to build artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T10:33:40-08:00","id":373607,"title":"","content":"the bigger issue is crafting materials. If you had enough oricalcum to craft a longbow you wouldn't be in your current quest for the manse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T10:43:11-08:00","id":373614,"title":"","content":"Well, we are about to rob a bank. And there is a big ship-eating mountain filled with Magical Materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T14:52:16-08:00","id":373806,"title":"","content":"Huh, so I was re-reading restrictions on how to raise magitech and occult only needs to be 3 until making artifact 4+ things lore is what needs to always keep up with the craft. Adding that to the list of things I did wrong for too long. Oh god Mayu has an excuse to teach history to me we'll all doomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T15:09:30-08:00","id":373844,"title":"","content":"Actually, I imagine Mayu is a very good teacher. Her habit of spouting off boring fact at inappropriate times is more of a nervous habit. (She has two points in Socialize, but only two points in Charisma.)<br /> <br /> Unless you guys want her to be a boring professor type. Her character can go that way too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T16:18:23-08:00","id":373912,"title":"","content":"your character your rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T16:20:06-08:00","id":373914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=373844#post373844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I imagine Mayu is a very good teacher. Her habit of spouting off boring fact at inappropriate times is more of a nervous habit. (She has two points in Socialize, but only two points in Charisma.)<br /> <br /> Unless you guys want her to be a boring professor type. Her character can go that way too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always been a fan of sexy professor but thats just me.<br /> <br /> By the way if you haven't seen it yet I did a rough draft of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/373028-artifact-bioklave\">Bioklave</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T17:49:56-08:00","id":373939,"title":"","content":"I actually wrote down the new stats during the initial gathering on Friday. Btw I have an idea for the slimes, if I stole all of its essence via feeding or soul steel it might destabilize it or something since I'm stealing life energy. I'm also getting increasingly tempted to go for soul-cleaving wound if special enemies like this become a theme. Its costly so probably not though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T11:59:23-08:00","id":378263,"title":"","content":"8 or 8:30 tomorrow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T16:47:17-08:00","id":378451,"title":"","content":"8pm if it works for everyone. also to check you guys wanted to investigate the founders home right? Whats your secondary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T16:58:44-08:00","id":378457,"title":"","content":"We wanted to rob a bank!<br /> <br /> Also I think it was we wanted to find other manses in the city, instead of investigating the founder's home. (Unless the founder's home is a manse, then we might check it out).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:47:36-08:00","id":378548,"title":"","content":"I wanted to find everything possible and kill the slimes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T19:17:03-08:00","id":378605,"title":"","content":"8:30 for me.<br /> <br /> I'd like to take a look at the bank and see if we can find the second Manse as secondary things. <br /> <br /> If we don't find another chunk of orichalcum, we'll have to destroy a very valuable artifact which will cause Alric some personal pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T20:46:07-08:00","id":378640,"title":"","content":"good thing I asked.<br /> <br /> There is a way to kill the slimes and there was a hint. In truth I'm hoping saying there was a hint will get you thinking because truth is I did a horrible job trying to nudge you to it so I really screwed up. I also hope they are more interesting and challenging than annoying. I like enemies that are more like puzzles than something you just throw dice at.<br /> <br /> As a heads up, they are unique to here. Since they can easily be stored and deployed they are however a common base security measure within the city. I'm tempted to ramp up your enemies in the city and a bank makes a good excuse for more aggressive security. Robbing a bank will not be easy and far riskier. Houses and libraries focus on the safety of those inside. A bank will focus on making sure you dont get away<br /> <br /> I think with the current group make-up the most logical way for you guys to approach things is non-combat with bloodless forming a solid fall back plan in things go bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T10:52:03-08:00","id":379194,"title":"","content":"So... Training stuff<br /> <br /> I know Mayu is interesting in learning athletics (So she doesn't have to be carried up and down cliffs anymore). Bloodless mentioned that he needed Lore to advance into more Craft Magitech. Is anyone's character interested in learning Old Realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https:/