 ride and sail as favored with only one dot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:49:25-08:00","id":416906,"title":"","content":"Well, he still has 65 xp to spend. He mentioned wanting to ride his bear familiar and maybe getting an air ship in the future. So I just favored those for right now (which requires a point). As he plays, he can decide if he wants to put points in them or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:03:20-08:00","id":416916,"title":"","content":"Here is my thought process:<br /> <br /> I know he wants to play a character decent at combat. I am unsure about what other aspects of playing a RP character he will enjoy, as he has never RP'ed before. In video games, he likes playing healing characters, but there really isn't a niche for that in Exlated. For his base character, I focused on combat abilities that I know he will use and dipped into some abilities and charms that sound cool (Presence, Athletics, Occult, Ride, etc) I added Sail because he seemed interested in an Air Ship (or Ice Ship). <br /> <br /> For his XP, I don't think he is going to spend them all (or any) on combat abilities. I am hoping that he will figure out what he likes to do over the course of a few games and spend that XP on that. <br /> <br /> I will also admit, I maxed out his Willpower with Build points. Mostly because if I regret not doing that for Mayu. If you are uncomfortable with that level of Min Maxing, I can take some points out of Willpower and put them into Skill points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:12:14-08:00","id":416921,"title":"","content":"Just keep in mind the logistical issues of having a bear around. The issues we had with Makoto just getting her around some places and the reason we got her at all is because Alric's horse couldn't handle the harsh weather. I am ok with it, but make sure its a big part of the character because familars are more of an accent to a character than a tool. Because at the solar level they aren't the best way to go (mechanically) to get those advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:15:27-08:00","id":416923,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about dropping the bear, to be honest. I already took War out of the character. The bear doesn't really fit with the background I wrote for Fade (which I need to clean up and send over sometime this week).<br /> <br /> It's really weird writing up a character for someone else. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T15:24:18-08:00","id":416927,"title":"","content":"So I updated the character.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-UiWxItb8fkZUVCZUYwNF9xdFE/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-U...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Here are the changes:<br /> <br /> -Dropped the Bear<br /> -Dropped Willpower down to 7<br /> -Dropped one of the Melee Charms<br /> <br /> -Changed Favored Ability from Ride to Linguistics<br /> -Added points to Linguistics and Sail<br /> -Added Salty Dog Method Charm<br /> -Added Contacts (Haslanti League)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-25-2015, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:30:11-08:00","id":417970,"title":"","content":"Alright thats more balanced. I read the backstory, the family heirloom was abit... yea but you did give it sufficient weight so I'll give it a pass. By the sounds of it he is a &quot;punish gods that abuse their station&quot; type which is is a fine motivation and I can see it fitting into a combat zenith. Might still need to work out how to integrate him into the game though. I'd like to figure out something more narratively interesting than &quot;he just happens upon you guys&quot;. Maybe do some side stuff with him to get a feel for the character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T14:40:48-08:00","id":418000,"title":"","content":"Yeah. The Heirloom part was a bit heavy handed. I'm not really good at writing in magic swords into backgrounds.<br /> <br /> I did have this crazy idea that Fade ran into Makoto and Makoto, curious about what a Solar can actually do, ran him though some situations to test him. Makoto wouldn't so something like that to his little sister. Some random Solar? Totally. I think Brandon is going to play him pretty clear cut, (I think. He's never Role Played before, so it could be interesting.) so maybe he sends him Mayu's way. A Zenith with a military background is a much more suitable companion for his sister than the naked thief and the lazy sleeping dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T01:31:21-08:00","id":418510,"title":"","content":"Don't forget to get him a mundane sword. Pretty darn sure the wyld hunt have killed a few anathema whom claim to have a trade associated with a weapon they've never been seen to use or even have. Also I'm going to be drawing more than one exalt to this fight so he might not have to wait long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:52:41-08:00","id":418662,"title":"","content":"So I updated his character sheet. Added a Chopping Sword and a Knife. I also beefed up his intimacies. Added the Heirloom Sword and the Storm God of the White Sea (Negative). Figured the god that Fade intimated is still around and is mighty embarrassed by being told off by this upstart Solar. Also Fade doesn't have the dice pool of the Unconquered Sun to intimated the god anymore. I foresee massive sea storms and the like to make good use of Fade's Sail Skill. <br /> <br /> I did consider making Fade's Great grandfather a Lunar. But I'm pretty sure that Lunar don't really run around with Diaklaves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T12:57:31-08:00","id":419225,"title":"","content":"Depends on the lunar honestly, it's tricky to use the bigger artifacts because they lack dedicated weapon/armor elsewhere charms but if it can be used by many pockets meditation the're solid (also tattoo artifacts are awesome). A good way for Brandon to flesh out his character personally is have him name the exact emotion that is tied to the intimacy. For instance, Bloodless has a negative intimacy of weariness with dragon-blooded, while a blanket negative intimacy would imply he highly dislikes or hates them. If we ever convert to 3rd edition this will make it a bit easier as intimacies will be really important instead of just a minor thing. This is kind of why it takes me all day to make a character, I'll sit and ponder multiple choices for all of this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T13:09:05-08:00","id":419238,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I figured he could figure all that stuff out as he learns how to play. Brandon is a learn by doing kind of person. He has never RP'ed before and has only heard one side of our Exalted games and my Pathfinder game. When I asked him about motivations and Intimacies, he didn't really understand how they impacted game play. Let him play, figure out how to play his character, and then flesh out his character sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T06:47:03-08:00","id":422866,"title":"","content":"Two things I forgot to mention last night:<br /> <br /> 1. When Alric gets back to the house finally, I would like to check on Makoto and Yolo to see how they are<br /> <br /> 2. When out doing his Batman impersonation, I'll be bringing the Daiklaves, but not using them unless necessary (ie. things knives can't hurt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T09:29:20-08:00","id":423035,"title":"","content":"Thing 3:<br /> <br /> I will not be able to make it on March 20th; my parents are coming for the weekend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T14:28:40-08:00","id":423440,"title":"","content":"actually that reminds me, do you have spirit cutting or ghost eating technique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T16:41:28-08:00","id":423557,"title":"","content":"Nope. I'm hoping Orichalcum will help in some cases, but I think I'll only be able to do something about the walking dead. Actual incorporeal ghosts might not be something I can address. I'm operating under the assumption that Alric isn't all that supernaturally aware, so there will undoubtedly be some surprises. I don't know if Mayu has those charms, but I can probably rope her in if she does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:11:23-08:00","id":423647,"title":"","content":"Mayu has Spirit cutting attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T18:15:47-08:00","id":423650,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be stocking up on a lot of resistance charms for a while so a lucky pot shot doesn't make things super stressfull. that &quot;necromancer&quot; will be getting a lot of money though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T07:21:16-08:00","id":424130,"title":"","content":"So I've discovered something really weird, there's a charm called stitched flesh resilience in anathema that says it's from scroll of errata but for the life of me I couldn't find it, so I start googling and low and behold there are multiple references to it. Turns out that stitched flesh resilience is the mirror to ox-body mastery and accidently got cut out in the update to the scroll of errata that happened forever ago. Really makes you wonder how often great charm concepts are lost by a whim of fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:13:16-08:00","id":424317,"title":"","content":"So... Brandon decided not to play. So no Zenith for us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:51:50-08:00","id":424662,"title":"","content":"so close! : C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:52:13-08:00","id":424663,"title":"","content":"aww, and I finally figured out how to integrate him<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spaaace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=423557#post423557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I'm hoping Orichalcum will help in some cases, but I think I'll only be able to do something about the walking dead. Actual incorporeal ghosts might not be something I can address. I'm operating under the assumption that Alric isn't all that supernaturally aware, so there will undoubtedly be some surprises. I don't know if Mayu has those charms, but I can probably rope her in if she does.</div> </div> </div> </div>orichalcum wont help you strike immaterial. Nor does it aid in the fact ghosts can (though not always) reform if slain. So you could temporarily deal with them but cutting them up is not a permanent solution. This is also ooc just so you know the dead were rising because he was a midnight cast, zombies wont be a huge issue. Unless something is done to maintain or enhance them zombies degrade pretty fast and cant &quot;infect&quot; people. Even if you did nothing they'd be dead in a week. Of course trying to stomp them out purely for safety and giving the dead a proper burial is still a good idea. Hard for a ghost to pass on when his body is walking around attacking people","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:31:03-08:00","id":424695,"title":"","content":"&quot;We do what we must because we can.&quot;<br /> <br /> While it may have limited efficacy, I'm looking at this as an outlet for survivor's guilt. Bloodless was maimed and almost killed; Mayu was injured; Eve was maimed and her family heirloom was stolen. The town was devastated, zombies and hungry ghosts are rising up. Despite all this, Alric got through it all without even a scratch.<br /> <br /> It might be too late to save the town from destruction, but he will do what he can to keep it from getting worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T05:51:23-08:00","id":426483,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out there are thaumaturgy procedures that can help out dealing with ghosts for way cheaper than the 3 occult charms if you can stomach only being able to deal with a specific type of spirit. Unfortunately for some ungodly reason Anathema doesn't have a real slot for thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:15:09-08:00","id":430389,"title":"","content":"Game tonight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T10:23:11-08:00","id":430396,"title":"","content":"I hope so. I'll be there shortly after 8pm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:08:21-08:00","id":430479,"title":"","content":"yes, I just got home, took care of all my stuff, so now I can relax and think about what to toss at you guys next","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T06:44:02-07:00","id":433894,"title":"","content":"Is there room for another in the group? I am a log time rpg player (over 20 years) that has wanted to play Exalted since I got the books back in the 1st ed days but never had a chance. If there is still room what characters are in the group? Is it just the 3 listed on the 1st page? I have two concepts I have toyed with over the years. A Night Caste vigilante crime fighter type from Nexus, a dark and all business type demeanor, or a Twilight Caste (I think they are the scholar/crafter caste) Warrior Smith type guy big and burly with Axe/Hammer and shield, noble and jolly in demeanor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:12:09-07:00","id":434070,"title":"","content":"We have room for another and could probably fit another after that since 3 pc's is a little small (there used to be a fourth but scheduling got in the way) We game over Skype on Fridays 8-12pm EST. I'm a dusk martial artist that's also a crafter, we have a know it all twilight archer that's also getting craft and just picked up some medicine charms (crippling effects man), and lastly we have a short daiklaive wielding night caste that has gotten all the fun thief charm stuff (lock opening touch comes up more often than you'd think). Considering we already have 2 crafters your night caste concept would work better, although the idea of the party building artifacts while the resident night caste dies from boredom is hilarious. Oh, before I forget we do use 2.5 and no merit/flaws (the ST has gotten burned with flaw fishers).<br /> If you're still interested talk to Aeroz on sorting your character out. I'm pretty sure you'll be getting around 60'ish experience to play with as a catch up mechanism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:19:57-07:00","id":434078,"title":"","content":"One day, I will buy Linguistics charms for my Twilight. *Shakes Fist*<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:41:40-07:00","id":434097,"title":"","content":"Should be pretty soon unless sorcery/necromancy teaching rears its head just to annoy you. I still gotta dump 30+ experience so I don't crumble to a lucky shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:46:12-07:00","id":434099,"title":"","content":"I think I am going to buy the Second Medicine Excellency and then start collecting XP for Essence 4. Then buy Linguistics Charms!<br /> <br /> ...or more likely Archery Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:56:01-07:00","id":434104,"title":"","content":"Ugh... I need to get essence four too. Stupid high experience cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:04:28-07:00","id":434114,"title":"","content":"Ok probably will go with the night Caste then and play up being an investigator crime fighter type so to differentiate from the thief, Probably gonna need some help with character creation especially charms since I have never actually had any play time with exalted and y'all are already a good ways in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:14:01-07:00","id":434127,"title":"","content":"I'd make a base character and play for a game or two and then spend your extra XP. <br /> <br /> The Investigation Charms are mostly about reading people. Our thief uses those charms to see who is worth stealing from. There is one charm for searching a room called Crafty Observation Method. It allows you to do a fifteen minute search in a few seconds.<br /> <br /> Athletics has some really amazing charms, too many to list. If I had to rebuild my character again, I would have favored Athletics. <br /> <br /> All the tracking charms are in Survival. City-Moving Secrets is a good one for your concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:36:59-07:00","id":434161,"title":"","content":"Some charms to consider for investigative work: sagacious reading of intent-linguistics, Mastery of small Manners-Socialize, most investigation charms, keen (sense) technique-awareness. Thunderbolt attack prana-athletics and enemy castigating solar judgment- presence are good combat charms if you don't feel too enamored going deep in the standard combat trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:08:11-07:00","id":434215,"title":"","content":"Hey there,<br /> <br /> My only concern is whether your vigilante concept will cause too much friction with our thief. Some conflict is fine; we have lots of fun interpersonal repartee going on, however if he's going to try and arrest another member of the group, that would be a problem.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would rather have another competent fighter than to worry about a third crafter. And, a jolly fellow to go carousing alongside would be better than the mopey sticks in the mud that are the other characters. (I kid, I kid... =D )<br /> <br /> Hmm... I guess the best thing to take is what you think would be fun. Here's a little about the game as opposed to the characters:<br /> <br /> We're in a large city in the north (an invention of the GM, AFAIK) where Mayu (archer/Twilight) lives. We met on the run from some Dragon Blooded who may or may not have been Wyld Hunt and we're not sure which of us they were after. They may or may not be still after us. We've run into and interfered with the plans of a rival Deathlord, so I expect there will be further Abyssal/Deathlord/Underworld plotlines. We've been even further north to discover an abandoned, intact, biotech first age city and we're currently working out how to control and/or exploit it. After our return from the first age city, Bloodless' deathlord sent a goon to collect the runaway Abyssal but relented after wrecking half the city under the impression that Bloodless was working on converting the other members of the group to the Deathlord's service (not actually happening?) We're currently fighting off the resulting Hungry Ghosts and trying to prevent the city from turning into a shadowland.<br /> <br /> That's about it in a nutshell. Mayu, Bloodless, feel free to expand if you think I've missed anything.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:28:50-07:00","id":434268,"title":"","content":"The Local Deathlord has a train and we're in the north, on the south coast of the white sea (not on the glacier).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T11:55:37-07:00","id":434345,"title":"","content":"Spaaace has given you a pretty good summary of what has happened so far. <br /> <br /> My Twilight is pretty focused on Lore, Investigation, Awareness. Mayu is already rolling massive dice pools for finding and figuring stuff out. <br /> <br /> The more I think about it, I don't mind there being another crafter. I picked up some crafting to make things to further my character's goals than for my character to be a crafter. Though Bloodless (the Abyssal character) can only craft things that cause death (weapons) or else he will gain resonance. <br /> <br /> A bit more about our character personalities and niches:<br /> <br /> Mayu is a spirited, slightly idealistic, young woman from Lookshy. She is a big know it all and if she doesn't know it, she can figure it out. Her niche is finding things out and range sniper attacks.<br /> <br /> Alric is the charming but womanizing thief/gambler. If Alric can't swindle something out someone, he will simple steal it. He also can get into anywhere or anything. Sometime, Mayu has to ride piggyback to be able to follow the other two players.<br /> <br /> Bloodless is the stoic, mysterious type that likes to eat food offered by our enemies and sleeps a lot. He is also very good at breaking things or people. The two Solars are like &quot;Hey, this guy is our friend and he is cool!,&quot; until he does some scary abyssal crap. And then we are like &quot;What have we done!?!&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:28:25-07:00","id":434403,"title":"","content":"Well then my night would be like a mix of Mayu and Alric it seems but I think he and Alric would get a long as he is more concerned with the big bad guys and crime groups as opposed to individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:30:10-07:00","id":434405,"title":"","content":"What parts of investigation are you focusing Mayu? Like Charm wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:49:31-07:00","id":434416,"title":"","content":"Mayu has Crafty Observation Method. She is not a high social character, so I haven't picked up any of the observing individuals charms. She also has Keen Sight Technique from the Awareness charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:05:21-07:00","id":434442,"title":"","content":"Ok well I looking into like interrogation, like judge's ear and such, and tracking and possibly some presence stuff for intimidation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:09:06-07:00","id":435799,"title":"","content":"So far this is what I am coming up with a Large powerfully built Northman that was a bounty hunter/Big Game hunter, I bit of a general problem solver focused on hunting things down. That has exalted as a Night Caste and fights with twin hatchets. Got most everything done but my Charms there are so many that I want and so few slots...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:17:14-07:00","id":435886,"title":"","content":"My advice is to prefer fundamentals over the flashy cool charms, mainly because those fundamental charms will be used a hell of a lot more then the flashy charms (it's still okay to grab a few flashy ones because the're fun). I usually end up buying 2-3 charms with bonus points as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:52:35-07:00","id":435941,"title":"","content":"Charm Excellencies are amazing. Don't forget about them!<br /> <br /> Don't forget to send your backstory to Aeroz for approval. He will probably have some comments and suggestions for your character. PMing him would probably work best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:50:30-07:00","id":436177,"title":"","content":"Yeah been talking to Areoz on Skype some. Trying to keep charms to basics but still needing like 16-18 charms and bonus points all going to essence 3 resources and a lot of skill points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5280-gfrobbin84","name":"gfrobbin84","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:13:31-07:00","id":436725,"title":"","content":"OK so still got to write up my backstory and get ap