xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T00:50:56-07:00","id":499973,"title":"","content":"So when xenos gets his character approved and is waiting for his character to be written in. Does he get exp for those games if he's there? Also I'm hoping this conflict doesn't come to blows, considering this is a second circle that's on the upper eidolons of that rank's power. The small myriad of terrestrial martial artists and the possible celestial lieutenant will probably make him beatable, but people will die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T06:02:14-07:00","id":502826,"title":"","content":"For Aeroz:<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?t=21&amp;v=sdXTO0pR2zM\" data-code=\"sdXTO0pR2zM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/sdXTO0pR2zM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T08:48:53-07:00","id":506894,"title":"","content":"So, I was thinking about this Demon Lord. I think we need to try to bargain with him. See what he wants. Mayu won't like it but having the other passengers die isn't an acceptable option to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T09:27:23-07:00","id":506938,"title":"","content":"The first thing to find out is why the hell a second circle cares if a couple first circle subordinates die. He likes to monologue, I say let him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T15:21:04-07:00","id":507270,"title":"","content":"as a heads up, I'm working abit late, so expect to start later tomorrow, probably closer to 9pm EST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T18:51:07-07:00","id":507472,"title":"","content":"If that's the case, I might actually be around by then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:16:13-07:00","id":507488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=506938#post506938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first thing to find out is why the hell a second circle cares if a couple first circle subordinates die. He likes to monologue, I say let him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing the answer is that it gives him the excuse to harass some Solaroids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:18:57-07:00","id":507492,"title":"","content":"I have something in mind and you guys will either find it very cool or very lame","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:42:34-07:00","id":507511,"title":"","content":"Can it be both?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T09:35:24-07:00","id":508161,"title":"","content":"can something be both? yes. Can this be both? no","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T16:39:50-07:00","id":508550,"title":"","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've come down with a cold or something today. I'll be online for the start of the game, but no guarantees how long I'll last.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:11:55-07:00","id":509261,"title":"","content":"Hey all,<br /> <br /> Rumor (i.e. Xeno426) has it you've got room for one more. Would anyone object to a sorcerer joining the group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5982-circlmastr","name":"CirclMastr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T18:15:27-07:00","id":509357,"title":"","content":"yes there is room for a fifth pc, but there was also someone else wanting to listen in as well. We doubt they'll actually join as they're a coworker who's never messed with rpg's and exalted isn't exactly newb friendly. So you'll likely be able to join but just thought you should know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:00:35-07:00","id":513378,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone, i have also expressed interest in possibly joining you game, and in order to facilitate that, i would like to know what type of characters everyone has and what type of character they would like to see join the group. Also, a quick rundown of where you are and what your goals are, would also help facilitate the creation of a character who is both useful and can easily slide into the group with as little friction as possible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> i look forward to hopefully joining your band of intrepid heros and having a good time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. if anyone needs/wants to contact me on skype for any reason i am ( hemophage1 ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2741-hemophage","name":"Hemophage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:02:36-07:00","id":514117,"title":"","content":"My girlfriend and myself are interested in joining the game. We've both played a long time and I've run and am currently running a game. I'd really look forward to the chance to play in a game (a rare thing for me). I've got several characters that I could adapt to the setting and it's always fun coming up with new concepts as well. If you let us in, I'd probably play as a Infernal/Lunar and she'd play as a Solar/Abyssal but could play a Lunar. I always use Obsidian Portal to keep all the info for my games - I would welcome the chance to provide such a resource for your game as well.<br /> <br /> On Skype, my profile is provided via PM.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T20:46:07-07:00","id":514757,"title":"","content":"Ok, there is a sudden influx of interested parties and I have been dealing with a small animal so I haven't been on alot. I decided I will do this as a second round of recruiting.<br /> <br /> From my existing players please describe your character and your main plans as far as stats. Since your paths have changed and you have been working to cover gaps I am not 100% on where you guys intend to go with them<br /> <br /> As for the new interested parties, this has gotten out of hand so I'm making two things clear. This is a heroic game, the PCs aren't saints by a long shot but they ultimately work to help people. Secondly. I am only accepting solars. Frankly I should have had a firm stance on this from the start as its caused quite a few issues.<br /> <br /> In any case PM me if you'd like to sit in on a session to get a feel for the group. To be clear even if you did PM me already do it again so I know you are still interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T05:53:14-07:00","id":515091,"title":"","content":"The game I'm running has: 1 Solar, 1 TAW Lunar, 2 Infernals and an Abyssal. Have not really had issues, even with the players working with their benefactors - the PC's don't have all the meta-knowledge. They have to take everything at face value, the typical person knows nothing about a Deathlord, other than that it controls a large area of the Underworld, other than that they could be benign or malicious. The Silver Pact can hide and act through proxies without ever being known or mentioned. The Yozi are a little harder, some patrons perhaps untenable, like Malfeas, but many are very workable in most any game (Ebon Dragon, SWLiHN and Szoreny come to mind).<br /> <br /> I'll monitor this thread, but I've never been big on Black and White games (you act when you believe in something - not because you're a hero) and Solars are extremely bland to me. Their charms have no interesting cracks or gaps, just perfects and instants and static dice bonuses. I'd much rather have charms with flavor and theme but a few cracks. Interested to hear the other PC's stories and motivations per current time though - that'll be a good window to the game for all us outsiders <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":". 05-15-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:28:44-07:00","id":515103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=514757#post514757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my existing players please describe your character and your main plans as far as stats. Since your paths have changed and you have been working to cover gaps I am not 100% on where you guys intend to go with them</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing Alric, a thief, gambler and womanizer from the North. Alric is a good sort, but has spent most of his life fending for himself so he's a bit aloof until you get to know him. He always keeps an escape plan (for himself) in mind in case things go south for the group, but won't admit to himself that he wouldn't abandon his companions. He's a smartass and not afraid of causing a little trouble. He's also a little loose with concepts of &quot;ownership&quot; or &quot;property&quot;. As the character least exposed to the supernatural world, he tends to operate as the voice of the uninitiated when dealing with weird stuff. Recently he's been finding he has some affinity for animals (mounts) and finds them to be good, loyal company that he's willing to defend.<br /> <br /> My main areas of long term character development are Athletics, Larceny, Ride, Investigation and Socialize. I will be doing a little rounding out with Melee and Resistance in the short term.<br /> <br /> As for a Black and White game, I hope you're not getting the wrong opinion. This means we generally try to help people, or at a minimum don't make things worse. This doesn't always work out, however. What we are not is thugs, murderers or sociopaths. This is a heroic game, but they are flawed heroes. Much of the fun that I have in the game isn't the powers of the characters, though there's lots of amazing things you can do with the non-combat charms (Athletics especially), it's the interactions between contrary personalities and goals as we try to figure out what it is to be Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:41:23-07:00","id":515107,"title":"","content":"Just saying I prefer a Conan: stealing for wealth and wenches, killing for revenge and because its the best solution (for him), and working for the nobility because the pay is good.<br /> I have no liking for Supermen: Hiding identity to protect loved ones, helping people for no freaking reason, working for no on because he only works for the force of good. I mean it's really a shallow and extremely inhuman character.<br /> <br /> Sounds like your character is pretty pragmatic Spaaace, that cool. So what are three things he hopes to accomplish in the next five years? Or is he more of a live day to day sort?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:51:31-07:00","id":515111,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say that the game is black and white. The players are more the lighter shade of grey. None of us are Captain America (We had a character who was basically Captain America and he left the game.) As Aeroz said, we aren't saints, but we aren't the type to sit by and watch people suffer. This is a cliff notes version of how our characters operate:<br /> <br /> Mayu (Twilight): Oh noes! We did something to cause trouble for these people <i>(Because let's be honest, this is how it usually happens)</i>. We should fix this!<br /> Alric (Night): What? No! That is a bad idea! We need to get out of here! It's too much of a risk of exposing ourselves!<br /> Mayu and Alric: What do you think, Bloodless?<br /> Bloodless (Dusk): Umm..... *Goes and punches thing that is causing the problem* Does this help?<br /> <br /> So, yes. We fuck up...a lot. We are definitely flawed heroes (even without limit breaks). Mayu is a bit short sighted (ironically). Alric is a bit self centered. Bloodless is constantly fighting between his desire to not kill people and his abyssal nature. But at the end of the day, the three of us couldn't live with ourselves if we let people suffer for our actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, what Aeroz he asked for:<br /> <br /> Mayu is one of the many Twilight characters who exalted in Lookshy, though her primary focus isn't crafting. She sees crafting as a means to an end. Mayu is more of the scholarly type who was completely shocked at the general ignorance of everyone outside of the River Provinces. Her main motivation is to start distributing all the lost First Age lore that she has acquired since her exaltation and try to raise the general educational level of the population. As a first step, she wants to build a printing press and start writing books under a pseudonym. She also has some deal with a Library god to increase the number of libraries in Creation (a long term goal).<br /> <br /> Mayu is a bit trigger happy when it comes to the &quot;monsters&quot; of creation. If it is Fae, Demonic, or other dangerous looking creature, she will shoot first and ask questions later.<br /> <br /> As for skills, Mayu is a know it all (Lore, Occult). If she doesn't know, she will use Awareness and Investigation to find out. She is a very competent archer and relies on not getting hit in combat (Dodge).<br /> <br /> As for future plans, Mayu is going to be focusing on Archery and other Combat Charms. Then she will pick up some Linguistics Charms and All-Encompassing Sorcerer's Sight. After that, maybe flesh out her craft? Mayu is on the path to be initiated into Sorcery, but I doubt I am going to take anything besides the counter spell, the messenger spell, and maybe the floating platform. (I'm mostly doing the initiation for story reasons).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-15-2015, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:02:36-07:00","id":515116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515107#post515107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no liking for Supermen: Hiding identity to protect loved ones, helping people for no freaking reason, working for no on because he only works for the force of good. I mean it's really a shallow and extremely inhuman character.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been a plot point that Aeroz has been dangling in front of us for months about travelers being attacked by demons. We've barely touched it, until we became the travelers being attacked by demons. (If the two groups of demons are connected.)<br /> <br /> Mayu hides her identity to protect herself. Mayu might help an old lady cross the street if she isn't too busy with other stuff. (That is if she even notices the little old lady. Maybe if said old lady had cookies and Sidereal Charms to attract Mayu's attention).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-15-2015, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:10:51-07:00","id":515121,"title":"","content":"Gotcha Wonder. That's a pretty lofty goal, trying to educate Creation. I would imagine most people have never seen a book, probably 98% illiteracy rate outside of Realm and the River Provinces. Before people can learn about First Age lore, their is so much infrastructure to build up, books cost months if not years of a monks (typically a minor noble, second son yada yada) life and costs untold money. Most people do not speak the same language, endless dialects, the influence and power of the God of Written Knowledge is probably very minor and it might be fearful of angering it's long time worshipers (the lords and nobles - who would probably resist such an expensive movement for the power it takes out of their hands). Sounds like that would be an amazing personal story.<br /> <br /> Only question, where did the printing press come from? Did you find one in a manse? I trust it is one that does the print with a single page at a time, not movable type? Mostly tying to figure out if this is a example of, I know about this from the metagame, so want to use it as a watermark for my character in this game? Something like the printing press and it's invention should have a ton of story and scenes that build towards the moment of discovery. Either way, I like the challenges of education the East. That is the kinda motivation that takes decades or centuries - love seeing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:18:09-07:00","id":515126,"title":"","content":"I'm going to build the printing press! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thus crafting being the means to an end.<br /> <br /> I didn't make my character from Lookshy just to get access to all that sweet Magitech knowledge (though that is a pretty awesome perk). I just love the military culture and high standard of living. I wanted my character have this arrogance of Lookshy being the best place in creation and be recovering from a state of culture shock of how the rest of Creation lives.<br /> <br /> Yes. I doubt I'll get to fully accomplish my goal in game. But Mayu can work towards it. My characters usually have really long term goals. Mayu thinks she has about 200 years to accomplish this, so she thinks she can get the program off to a good start. Just wait until she finds out Solars can live thousands of years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:31:09-07:00","id":515134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515107#post515107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just saying I prefer a Conan: stealing for wealth and wenches, killing for revenge and because its the best solution (for him), and working for the nobility because the pay is good.<br /> I have no liking for Supermen: Hiding identity to protect loved ones, helping people for no freaking reason, working for no on because he only works for the force of good. I mean it's really a shallow and extremely inhuman character.<br /> <br /> Sounds like your character is pretty pragmatic Spaaace, that cool. So what are three things he hopes to accomplish in the next five years? Or is he more of a live day to day sort?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, for your Conan checklist we do it all:<br /> <br /> Stealing for wealth and wenches? Hell yeah!<br /> Killing for revenge because it's the best solution: Absolutely, but as revenge not because we wanted his table at the restaurant.<br /> Working for nobility because the pay is good: Absolutely, but again, we're not sociopaths so there are limits on what the nobility can buy from us. If the current bad Noble is the best option, then we'll work for him.<br /> <br /> Mostly our good deeds are a result of things we've messed up and some sense of personal responsibility compels us to clean up our own mess. We've walked away from bad people doing bad things because we didn't have a stake in the outcome. On the other hand, when a town was devastated by the Deathknight who Bloodless is rebelling from, we worked to keep the town from falling into a Shadowland and being overrun with hungry ghosts. If we hadn't been living there, the town wouldn't have been partially destroyed, so we stuck around to keep the worst at bay. Plus, there was some interesting character interactions between Alric/Mayu and Bloodless (the Abyssal) along the lines of &quot;WTF!&quot;<br /> <br /> As for Alric, he's more a go with the flow guy at the moment; life is good, money is easy, women are willing. Mostly this is because this is my first Exalted campaign so I didn't really have a big overarching goal. I'm still working on what my Epic goals will be. In the medium term, he's likely to support Mayu's desire to educate the planet and help get Bloodless out from under the thumb of the Deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:57:00-07:00","id":515168,"title":"","content":"Just for my own curiosity, why did you all decide to change it back to Solar only? I take it that the Deathlord/Abyssal stuff was a little straining for a bit, struggling with the dark side of the character and maybe Deathlord interaction taking a lot of the direction of the game on its shoulders? Or was it more a keeping a mechanical hand on the differences between Limit and Resonance/charms/and so on?<br /> <br /> Lunars are very close to Solars for an ethics and behavioral point of view. I mean, I don't even know if you'd have room for 2 more, but we have been looking at playing two lunars in a game for some time. Merchant Lunars, Vael the Gemling Prince and Merrik, who needs no fancy titles. Vael's family is from Rokan-Jin (hence the Gemling) but the family moved to Sijan and became merchant princes after liquidating much of their gem mines and other holdings, hence the prince.<br /> <br /> I know you guys have your own thing going on but let me link the stuffs anyways, maybe it will be an enjoyable read:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ccwvOypGTPuH55gY810Al8Qdmr4PLCCS-InWacSi3YY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Have a lot of other stuff written up, family tree, and such - but all of that is on the home computer. We would love to play Lunars, but I understand either way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T10:29:14-07:00","id":515269,"title":"","content":"Just warning you now, there's been a stigma about lunars in our game where they've all been assholes to us so it'd be a while before warming up to them. We still allow non-Solars it's just it's kind of weird to have two abyssals and the ST doesn't like how infernals are in 2.5 (we also had a guy try to min-max one which didn't help). We're having a sidereal join the group but remember the campaign is still solaroid level so you're going to feel the power disparity if you're fine with that.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should talk about Bloodless Totality of Obsidian now.<br /> Bloodless is a Dusk abyssal and ex-privateer that focus on killing things and building things to kill people (with a dash of necromancy) which makes it really hard to only kill people he intends to murder and not everyone in sight. Bloodless is originally from the west and is currently running from his Deathlord the Silver Prince and technically from his wife(Maeiv Cathak don't worry she's patrician and cut ties to the realm although it's possible for her to exalt kind of) and kid (Lethia) he abandoned when he exalted (whom he is still technically married to). His main goal is to get away from his Death lord's grasp and bulldoze any whom he sees as a threat without too much collateral damage. As a side quest Bloodless does want to learn malfean drinking songs though. <br /> <br /> Bloodless is surprisingly tolerant of supernatural things because mundane things tend to bother him more. Ultimately he is a very simple man with loyalties being built by good food and good company. <br /> <br /> His focuses are Martial arts, a dash of war, occult of the necromancy variety, resistance (soak build), craft, and he's currently trying to improve either his integrity, athletics, or learning more than one necromancy spell.<br /> <br /> Oh, Bloodless doesn't like to talk preferring to use a menagerie of stares and facial expressions to communicate where possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:02:20-07:00","id":515301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515269#post515269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We're having a sidereal join the group but remember the campaign is still solaroid level so you're going to feel the power disparity if you're fine with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine with that, though, if TAW is allowed - we like it a lot better than Core. They never got around to a Lunar Errata and it always got the least charms from Ink Monkeys and otherwise.<br /> <br /> I never min/max or try to make some over powered bloated monster. My Touch of Sepia character is a Lunar painter, another merchant, she was not over powered in the least. I prefer my power to come from interpersonal relationships with npcs, totally within the hands of the ST.<br /> <br /> Social/Int is my go to character type. Int tends to be Merrik's preferred play style, though I doubt a merchant could get by without a little moxie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:10:25-07:00","id":515335,"title":"","content":"I've never read TAW so I have no idea if it's good/bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T13:22:46-07:00","id":515397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515335#post515335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never read TAW so I have no idea if it's good/bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Core Lunars have almost no Mental/Social charms. It all falls down into a pretty kitty combo and no one bothers with a mental build at all. So Core sees Beastman rere-hulk out and kill Lunars or Pretty Kitty and nothing else. TAW allows them to actually play as Attribute Exalts and have the tools to build around the characters story, rather than force yourself down these two narrow charm trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":". 05-15-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T15:44:07-07:00","id":515512,"title":"","content":"I appreciate everyones descriptions it helps a bunch. (Insert Name Here) &quot;Steve&quot; for now. Steve is the eldest son of a wealthy merchant family. They have a sprawling estate ~500 miles north west of Nexus, and south of Sijan, which was basically a serfdom. His family was secretly a yozis cult, spreading their &quot;faith&quot; to the surrounding peasantry. Steve Exalted as a Zenith, purging the darkness that had infected his family and exposing everyone to the truth of the Unconquered Sun. He has decided to use his gifted trade acumen and ties with the guild to expand his wealth and use his expanding wealth to undermine and remove the false immaculate religions and restore the brilliance and radiance of the one true faith. He is going to be well rounded, but will be specializing in Performance, Presence, Socialize, and Bureacracy and Larceny. Despite his somewhat ruthless and successful trading talents, he was very well liked by everyone (at least before his exaltation). Even those with whom he was especially cut throat during negotiations enjoyed his company, if not the results of the contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2741-hemophage","name":"Hemophage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T16:13:44-07:00","id":515573,"title":"","content":"Home, so I can upload the family tree. Looks like I have the other family members still bound up in paper - hoping to rectify that soon:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/i31ilLW\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/i31ilLW.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> If you are doing a game tonight we'd like to listen in, but whatever the plan is, just saying we have Friday night open for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6024,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","user":"Touch_of_Sepia","date":". 05-15-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:23:54-07:00","id":515617,"title":"","content":"This is after a two year haitus from exalted. I'm even rusty on solar and abyssal charms. I have no idea what TAW is.<br /> <br /> Actually the abyssal thing is working as intended. I told him from the start, you can play an abyssal but you will suffer for it. We didn't play things softly, resonance bites, he always makes people uncomfortable, his deathly nature raises alot of alarms, his deathlord makes trouble for the group. He lost a two dot artifact, his voice (restored) and his eye. However when I open up to other splats I am also hit with &quot;fixes&quot; and alt rules and after such a long time away from the table this really makes me weary. I even omitted most of my own house rules for this reason. If you want to play another splat, its with all the flaws and weaknesses that comes with them. An aspect of the story for a mixed game is the power imbalance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T17:43:14-07:00","id":515632,"title":"","content":"I've been playing the last six years and been active on the forums and Exalted reddit. I've run two successful games and played in a 4 year campaign - my partner in a far longer one. I did not bring up TAW as a point of balance or power. It's an issue of Core being a poorly *written* splat. Just like how Sidereals are extremely poorly written. <br /> <br /> It should be clear that you can not play a Mental Lunar in core, you can only *abuse* appearance if you play a Social Lunar in core, and 99% of people play soak monkey Beastman Transformation beat-face Lunars with Core. I've no interest in playing an over-powered Appearance Lunar that reduces all the other PC's and NPC's to 0 MDV. I would like to play a Mental/Social Lunar and that's not possible under Core. <br /> <br /> If you've been away from the scene awhile, would it not be a good idea to take the fixes from someone who's been here in your absence. I can help get you to speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T18:05:04-07:00","id":515657,"title":"","content":"Its not a matter of me catching up, its a matter of time. That and I do not want arguing or conflicting or getting flooded with custom materials. I wouldn't say I'm strict, its more we care more about story and just keeping things going. We aren't that crunchy. So no TAW. 2.5 as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T20:18:00-07:00","id":515703,"title":"","content":"I'll figure out a way to make Core Lunars work then - if you would let us sit in some time and/or talk on skype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T21:15:31-07:00","id":515785,"title":"","content":"Oh, Mayu. Try to do the right thing and talk to the guy and the NPC burns the place down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T08:49:47-07:00","id":516218,"title":"","content":"Dont think on it too much. This was meant as abit of a breather and interesting set piece since you guys will be in Sijan soon and it will be a massive multi-session game. I just hope I can work in the plot satisfactory","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:26:06-07:00","id":516237,"title":"","content":"I know. I just find it funny. It will give Alric ammunition the next time Mayu wants to try to be honest with someone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:43:17-07:00","id":516247,"title":"","content":"Remember the last time we helped someone? *house in flames*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T09:52:53-07:00","id":516255,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Things our circle has destroyed though good intentions</u></b><br /> - Invite poor Abyssal to circle - Half the City of Twisted Stone is destroyed and almost becomes a shadow land<br /> - Help poor Half Caste Lunar leave his house - Half Caste burns house down.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I'm missing some....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T11:53:28-07:00","id":516370,"title":"","content":"I had a god-blood of a thermal spring god get up to some interesting antics before. Shooting blasts of super heated water at PC's and getting locked up. Eventually they just sold him back to the god he'd pissed off. Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:09:57-07:00","id":516449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515301#post515301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They never got around to a Lunar Errata and <b>it always got the least charms from Ink Monkeys and otherwise.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals say hi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Touch_of_Sepia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=515397#post515397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and no one bothers with a mental build at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tried once years ago (before 2.5E). I was unimpressed. Also unimpressed with with casteless.<br /> <br /> Had a look at Terrifying Argent Witches (TAW), and it looks pretty cool, might actually make playing a Lunar interesting. I like the removal of the whole totem animal thing; Luna is a shapeshifter of everything, so it seemed odd that her chosen should all be comprise of animal shapes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T14:37:07-07:00","id":516493,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm fine with totems I just want more than just basic animals or for a way to change it. I always wanted to play a lunar who exalted in Malfeas and shape changed into demons without being ess 4+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:36:33-07:00","id":516576,"title":"","content":"Lotus of the Abyss is an awesome name for an abyssal martial artist. I'm considering making one just to use that name.<br /> <br /> Just sharing<br /> <br /> Anyways, just dont want this to actually discourage future good deeds. I kind of forgot about being able to talk to the dead so it put me in an odd spot. So I needed an out and liked the idea of him just snapping. I will also be honest that I worried your less honest natures would eventually get the better of you and you'd rob the poor guy. Another reason I dislike murder hobos is it creates too huge of a risk of players ransacking a place. If you guys played like that I couldn't have even done this idea<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:47:11-07:00","id":516581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=516576#post516576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, just dont want this to actually discourage future good deeds. I kind of forgot about being able to talk to the dead so it put me in an odd spot. So I needed an out and liked the idea of him just snapping. I will also be honest that I worried your less honest natures would eventually get the better of you and you'd rob the poor guy. Another reason I dislike murder hobos is it creates too huge of a risk of players ransacking a place. If you guys played like that I couldn't have even done this idea</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think you could talk to the dead if the soul had already gone on to Lethe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5492-xeno426","name":"Xeno426","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5492_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:49:00-07:00","id":516582,"title":"","content":"To be honest, the whole scenario felt like Murder Hobo bait. Out of character, I'm fine with the guy burning down the house. It is his house to burn down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T17:56:02-07:00","id":516591,"title":"","content":"And since it's burning down <i>anyways</i>, he shouldn't miss a couple of items... =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T00:13:38-07:00","id":516825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xeno426</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=516581#post516581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think you could talk to the dead if the soul had already gone on to Lethe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was not there, so I'm sure I missed things, but I think it tends to take 4ish days after death for this to occur. After 4ish days the upper and lower soul separate and the higher soul can go to Lethe, if the lower soul is appeased, no problems from it either. If you act fast, you can always ask the ghost some questions. Bloody Handed Gods do this to investigate murders - but sometimes people deal with the ghost (like a Zenith could do or a Necromancer to grease the gears).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6024-touch_of_sepia","name":"Touch_of_Sepia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6024_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T04:46:57-07:00","id":516933,"title":"","content":"Since we're discussing expansions to the game, what about Ink Monkeys? Enthusiastic yes, definite no, or case-by-case basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T06:14:07-07:00","id":516978,"title":"","content":"The Ghost was a Lunar, so he stuck around to continue exploring the underworld. <br /> <br /> I assume Ink Monkeys is a case by case basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:38:49-07:00","id":517163,"title":"","content":"Ink Monkeys right now is a no. Some stuff in there is, in my opinion, pretty broken. Other stuff isn't, but you know how busy I am right now and we are trying to integrate new players. If you want something from Ink Monkeys mention it to me in a month or two when things have hopefully stabilized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:57:06-07:00","id":517182,"title":"","content":"Bloodless has summon ghost (necromancer) and Aeroz rolled a chance die to see if his ghost was still wandering around, turns out it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T10:23:17-07:00","id":521999,"title":"","content":"so turns out someone picked this weekend to steal stuff out of my car. So not sure I'll get to much for the potential new people as that ate up some time. I still need to file a police report. Honestly its not a huge time consuming thing but with no days off and the kit its eating up alot of the spare time I have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T14:38:59-07:00","id":522561,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That sucks! Did they take anything important?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T18:38:14-07:00","id":522747,"title":"","content":"my ipod, which I couldn't wipe, and now I have to get in my car with nothing but dead silence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T05:46:31-07:00","id":523116,"title":"","content":"Sorry to hear that, Aeroz. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:40:18-07:00","id":523470,"title":"","content":"People have been trying to pull that crap in my neighborhood for a few years now, apparently the iPod cords sell for a bit as well, as my dad has probably lost like 5 now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:00:28-07:00","id":523488,"title":"","content":"I lost my ipod when my bag was stolen in college. It sucked walking to work/class without it.<br /> <br /> Reminder that I am going to be missing game tomorrow. I have people coming over Friday night and going to Comicpalooza the next day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:30:52-07:00","id":523664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=523470#post523470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People have been trying to pull that crap in my neighborhood for a few years now, apparently the iPod cords sell for a bit as well, as my dad has probably lost like 5 now.</div> </div> </div> </div>they did steal the cord but I have a back-up and from being left in the car through winter and spring the plastic housing was in pieces anyways","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T11:00:24-07:00","id":524578,"title":"","content":"just as a heads up, game is on for 8;00 pm EST today. after this session if players are still interested I will be taking submissions with 125 exp. To help you here is abit of what I am looking for and what I am not. SO here is Aeroz 7 vice and virtue for joining our game<br /> <br /> To get approved:<br /> 1. Characters that mesh with the group, meaning if you have an issue with Lookshy, or are a slaver, or something like that there would be too much inter-character conflict. I dont mind conflict but there is a point where they simply wouldn't join together.<br /> <br /> 2. Builds that dont step on any toes. We got our warrior dusk, scholarly twilight, and rogue night. There can be some cross-over (I expect everyone to be decent at combat) but we have some gaping holes to fill and people that do that get priority<br /> <br /> 3. Be interesting. If I explain it I'll just be eliminating possible ideas so I'll assume you know what I mean. So I better not see &quot;my exalted memories lead me to my manse with all these artifacts&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. Speak rivertongue, skytongue, sea tongue, or old realm. Otherwise no one will understand you. I suggest rivertongue as we are in the area<br /> <br /> 5. Be concise. Remember I'm busy and have to juggle keeping things going for current players and looking over your stuff. Give me a 3 page backstory and you will be shoved to the back of the line. If you have a child I just need to know you have a child, not their age, temperament, and favorite food. Focus on need to know information that gives a good overview overview of who the character is.<br /> <br /> 6. Be a solar, cause this is meant to be a solar game, so bumps you to the front of the line.<br /> <br /> 7. Accept my judgements. If I say something is overpowered, don't try to argue how its not. If you try something like &quot;but X has similar ability&quot; then the only thing you might accomplish is getting me to ban that power too.<br /> <br /> To get you disqualified:<br /> 1. Min/max, just dont.<br /> <br /> 2. Come at me with custom material. I don't care if its for your character or setting ideas, again it adds more work for me that I dont need.<br /> <br /> 3. Consistant Skype issues, while I hate to put this on here fact of the matter is if we cant get you into the group chat you cant play. So far this hasn't come up but you never know.<br /> <br /> 4. Meta-gaming and using ooc info. Its ok if you know, not if your character does. Also keep in mind I will alter things to suit my needs. I'll move entire cities if its for the sake of the story.<br /> <br /> 5. Overly IC is the counter-issue. &quot;But my character would do this&quot;, I dont care. If it hurts the story, if it ruins other peoples fun, you don't do it.<br /> <br /> 6. Manipulating, coercing, subverting the other PCs. Don't try to get them to join your religion, dont try to use UMI, don't pretend to be another splat, don't blackmail the other players, you get the idea.<br /> <br /> 7. Failure to read the above. Seriously don't come at me with a custom MA you want to use when I clearly stated just now no custom material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T01:52:06-07:00","id":526465,"title":"","content":"a summary for Mayu since she missed the game.<br /> Mostly setup, we got to Sijian, walked by a psychopath (whom I probably should've seen if she was a DK but oh well), turns out there's a tomb whom was related to my past life and waiting for calibration before summoning marquee for further information. Alric went snooping around investigating some super anti-dead weapon and turns out this mortar looking thing is really good at killing ghosts, turns out the weapons dealer is an orichalcum alchemical (or described as such) so Alric and I's characters are very confused as to how an artifact man is doing something seemingly antagonistic towards Death lords. Also Bloodless is wearing a Fox kabuki mask with a glorious blue mane because it's cool and is also wearing normal clothes because Sijian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T03:55:48-07:00","id":526521,"title":"","content":"Bloodless in normal clothes??? <br /> <br /> Thanks for the update!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:37:32-07:00","id":527055,"title":"","content":"Huh, I just realized only Mayu speaks river tongue and we're in Sijian where that's the main language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:19:55-07:00","id":527082,"title":"","content":"Alric does, he just doesn't want you guys to know he does, but now might be a good time to reveal that you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3945-aeroz","name":"Aeroz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T15:30:11-07:00","id":527089,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to want the charm where you can communicate regardless if you speak the same language for once in my life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3103-eura","name":"Eura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"663"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:01:34-07:00","id":527576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeroz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/265726-back-and-looking-to-play-skype-game-recruiting?p=527082#post527082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alric does, he just doesn't want you guys to know he does, but now might be a good time to reveal that you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should surprise exactly no one that Alric is not always forthcoming with inconsequential details. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3104-spaaace","name":"Spaaace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:04:14-07:00","id":527578,"tit